1
00:02:09,750 --> 00:02:13,300
Near 1299

2
00:02:15,285 --> 00:02:18,575
Episode 90

3
00:02:55,885 --> 00:02:57,385
Sons.

4
00:03:00,255 --> 00:03:04,955
This is İnegöl Castle.

5
00:03:10,335 --> 00:03:12,335
Look at it carefully.

6
00:03:13,605 --> 00:03:14,905
Carefully.

7
00:03:15,605 --> 00:03:19,185
We'll march there first.

8
00:03:20,355 --> 00:03:21,605
Then...

9
00:03:22,285 --> 00:03:26,765
we have Bursa, protected
by Keşiş Mountains.

10
00:03:27,635 --> 00:03:29,885
then, Constantinople...

11
00:03:31,355 --> 00:03:37,315
and then, the whole world.

12
00:03:40,935 --> 00:03:43,755
I took this cause from my father...

13
00:03:43,965 --> 00:03:46,555
and you will leave it to your children.

14
00:03:46,785 --> 00:03:53,815
And they will leave it to their
children.

15
00:03:56,485 --> 00:03:58,205
We'll become a state.

16
00:03:59,435 --> 00:04:01,455
We'll have endless campaigns.

17
00:04:02,335 --> 00:04:04,335
We'll have endless battles.

18
00:04:05,985 --> 00:04:07,485
My children.

19
00:04:08,035 --> 00:04:09,855
We were born on horseback...

20
00:04:10,285 --> 00:04:12,105
we'll die on horseback.

21
00:04:12,585 --> 00:04:14,405
A horse is our purpose.

22
00:04:15,755 --> 00:04:17,635
A horse is the wings of Turks.

23
00:04:18,704 --> 00:04:23,515
And when we mount a horse...

24
00:04:23,955 --> 00:04:26,115
we always go forward!

25
00:04:26,455 --> 00:04:29,055
We always crave a campaign...

26
00:04:29,635 --> 00:04:32,555
we always want conquest.

27
00:04:33,255 --> 00:04:38,315
What takes us forward are two wings.

28
00:04:40,155 --> 00:04:43,265
Orhan, tell me.

29
00:04:43,955 --> 00:04:45,635
What is one of those wings?

30
00:04:45,835 --> 00:04:48,005
Cause of the world's order.

31
00:04:48,135 --> 00:04:50,205
Cause of the world's order.

32
00:04:52,655 --> 00:04:56,755
To bring Allah's order to the
whole world.

33
00:04:59,185 --> 00:05:00,505
Alahaddin.

34
00:05:01,685 --> 00:05:03,985
Tell me the other wing.

35
00:05:04,035 --> 00:05:06,055
Allah's words, father.

36
00:05:06,085 --> 00:05:07,615
Indeed.

37
00:05:07,755 --> 00:05:10,285
That's why we swing our swords.

38
00:05:10,285 --> 00:05:12,805
That's why we ride
our horses.

39
00:05:14,205 --> 00:05:18,035
And our cause is the cause
of Allah.

40
00:05:18,405 --> 00:05:21,235
Until the whole world is
ruled justly...

41
00:05:21,455 --> 00:05:24,885
until the oppressed have no
more to worry about...

42
00:05:26,885 --> 00:05:29,335
we'll be on the neck of the tyrants!

43
00:05:30,405 --> 00:05:31,955
My children!

44
00:05:35,755 --> 00:05:37,085
Come on!

45
00:05:37,885 --> 00:05:41,685
Let's gallop for our dreams!

46
00:05:54,495 --> 00:05:56,735
-Come on!
-Come on!

47
00:06:37,755 --> 00:06:40,255
Where will the passage
take us, father.

48
00:06:41,535 --> 00:06:44,385
There is an exit in every trouble.

49
00:06:44,485 --> 00:06:46,305
What's important is knowing
the way.

50
00:06:46,935 --> 00:06:49,505
If you know the way,
worry not.

51
00:06:49,515 --> 00:06:53,085
But if you don't, you should
take caution.

52
00:06:59,255 --> 00:07:00,635
Boran!

53
00:07:00,635 --> 00:07:01,955
My bey!

54
00:07:02,035 --> 00:07:03,355
Come.

55
00:07:05,555 --> 00:07:06,855
Go.

56
00:07:06,855 --> 00:07:08,355
Alright, my bey.

57
00:07:11,305 --> 00:07:12,675
Come on.

58
00:07:31,305 --> 00:07:32,805
My children.

59
00:08:24,755 --> 00:08:26,555
What is this place, father?

60
00:08:27,135 --> 00:08:29,905
The beginning of the road
to the conquest, Orhan.

61
00:08:33,804 --> 00:08:37,335
It's the den of the alps who
burn with the desire of jihad.

62
00:08:55,885 --> 00:08:57,705
All power to your elbow!

63
00:08:58,505 --> 00:09:00,535
Thank you, my bey.

64
00:09:00,955 --> 00:09:03,655
Thank you.
Thank you.

65
00:09:03,655 --> 00:09:05,405
Welcome, my bey.

66
00:09:06,485 --> 00:09:08,205
Salam Alaikum.

67
00:09:08,485 --> 00:09:10,515
-Alaikum Salam.
-All power to your elbow.

68
00:09:10,515 --> 00:09:12,435
Welcome, my bey.

69
00:09:13,035 --> 00:09:15,055
Thank you, Master Davud.

70
00:09:15,055 --> 00:09:17,105
Welcome, my shehzads.

71
00:09:17,105 --> 00:09:19,105
Thank you, Master Davud.

72
00:09:20,035 --> 00:09:21,605
Thank you, Master Davud.

73
00:09:21,605 --> 00:09:24,405
Tell me about the situation.

74
00:09:25,755 --> 00:09:27,555
Come, my bey.

75
00:09:32,455 --> 00:09:34,955
I've done all the calculations, my bey.

76
00:09:35,085 --> 00:09:37,155
The catapults will be
located like this.

77
00:09:38,155 --> 00:09:40,155
They will hit the walls...

78
00:09:40,155 --> 00:09:43,205
and these will destroy the gate,
inshallah.

79
00:09:51,235 --> 00:09:53,035
What about...

80
00:09:53,955 --> 00:09:56,835
the range of these catapults?

81
00:09:58,335 --> 00:10:00,535
They will be enough, my bey.

82
00:10:02,755 --> 00:10:04,985
If the wind blows the
opposite way...

83
00:10:05,155 --> 00:10:10,665
would they hit us instead?

84
00:10:10,905 --> 00:10:13,235
I knew that you would ask this, my bey.

85
00:10:13,685 --> 00:10:18,555
I strengthened the balls against
the wind.

86
00:10:19,805 --> 00:10:25,045
Allah's angels helped the warriors
of Bedr. If they help us too...

87
00:10:25,155 --> 00:10:28,005
no wind can stop us.

88
00:10:28,125 --> 00:10:29,705
Inshallah.
Inshallah.

89
00:10:30,485 --> 00:10:33,485
If we have the faith of the lions
of Bedr...

90
00:10:33,825 --> 00:10:38,075
the army of the angels will stand with us.

91
00:10:38,305 --> 00:10:40,365
Right, Mullah Alahaddin?

92
00:10:40,505 --> 00:10:42,305
True words, my bey.

93
00:10:42,335 --> 00:10:44,205
Mashallah.

94
00:10:45,685 --> 00:10:47,535
Mashallah to my valiant.

95
00:10:54,585 --> 00:10:55,905
My bey.

96
00:11:02,085 --> 00:11:03,635
Children.

97
00:11:10,055 --> 00:11:11,555
Tell me, Konur.

98
00:11:11,645 --> 00:11:12,985
My bey.

99
00:11:13,235 --> 00:11:17,455
As you ordered, Cerkutay has been
gathering intelligence.

100
00:11:18,155 --> 00:11:19,955
He is in İnegöl now.

101
00:11:20,585 --> 00:11:24,365
A troop is gathering weapons and
Rum Fire from Constantinople...

102
00:11:24,555 --> 00:11:26,635
to İnegöl.
They are almost there.

103
00:11:27,005 --> 00:11:29,085
But Cerkutay says that...

104
00:11:29,205 --> 00:11:31,075
if we don't stop the caravan...

105
00:11:31,405 --> 00:11:33,755
it will create great trouble for us.

106
00:11:37,605 --> 00:11:39,485
Weasel Nikola.

107
00:11:39,735 --> 00:11:42,955
Then, we'll strike at once.

108
00:11:44,205 --> 00:11:47,005
Wouldn't attacking a caravan break
the peace, my bey?

109
00:11:54,785 --> 00:11:57,605
That caravan has weapons, my shehzad.

110
00:11:58,635 --> 00:12:01,505
If they declare war on us
for attacking the caravan...

111
00:12:02,135 --> 00:12:05,685
he'll be guilty for gathering
ammunition in his castle.

112
00:12:10,385 --> 00:12:12,735
Nikola won't even see what's coming.

113
00:12:12,785 --> 00:12:15,285
We'll strike him like lightning.

114
00:12:16,785 --> 00:12:19,335
He won't even be able to chase it.

115
00:12:20,635 --> 00:12:22,835
We want to come too, my bey.

116
00:12:29,905 --> 00:12:32,755
You have the right.
Of course.

117
00:12:33,985 --> 00:12:37,185
But you aren't capable enough to
go to war yet.

118
00:12:38,235 --> 00:12:40,485
Prove yourself during hunting...

119
00:12:41,135 --> 00:12:43,705
then, I'll say that you are ready.

120
00:12:46,405 --> 00:12:47,905
Alright, my bey.

121
00:12:50,485 --> 00:12:53,005
Then, we need to hunt.

122
00:12:53,705 --> 00:12:55,035
Don't.

123
00:12:55,985 --> 00:12:58,505
Don't return empty handed.

124
00:13:01,255 --> 00:13:02,605
Don't.

125
00:13:03,105 --> 00:13:04,605
As you order, my bey.

126
00:13:06,805 --> 00:13:08,155
Baysungur.

127
00:13:08,185 --> 00:13:09,485
My bey.

128
00:13:09,685 --> 00:13:11,005
Come on.

129
00:13:22,185 --> 00:13:23,505
My bey.

130
00:13:23,605 --> 00:13:25,605
What about the gathering in Söğüt?

131
00:13:25,655 --> 00:13:28,205
Good. We won't go there empty-handed.

132
00:13:28,255 --> 00:13:31,755
But I'll go and position
early for the ambush.

133
00:13:32,835 --> 00:13:34,985
Don't be late.

134
00:13:36,985 --> 00:13:38,285
My bey.

135
00:13:38,455 --> 00:13:40,005
One of us should be with you.

136
00:13:40,035 --> 00:13:44,065
Allow me to ride alone.

137
00:13:54,645 --> 00:13:57,485
İnegöl Castle

138
00:14:06,985 --> 00:14:10,085
It looks like a valuable
fabric, Simon.

139
00:14:11,015 --> 00:14:13,065
It's very precious, sir.

140
00:14:13,115 --> 00:14:14,435
It's Chinese silk.

141
00:14:14,515 --> 00:14:17,365
It's a very old fabric,
left from Sasamis.

142
00:14:18,685 --> 00:14:22,255
They are using it to cover
the saints.

143
00:14:24,835 --> 00:14:26,865
Am I a saint, Simon?

144
00:14:27,065 --> 00:14:29,585
It's for the funerals of the saints.

145
00:14:29,585 --> 00:14:33,135
But you are standing next to me
like an ancient statue.

146
00:14:34,165 --> 00:14:36,235
You deserve it more than them.

147
00:14:55,635 --> 00:14:57,635
When will it come?

148
00:14:57,735 --> 00:14:59,515
It's on the way, sir.

149
00:15:00,315 --> 00:15:04,135
We have a peace treaty with
Osman.

150
00:15:04,185 --> 00:15:08,925
No one should know about
that ammunition.

151
00:15:09,015 --> 00:15:10,535
Do you get it?

152
00:15:10,595 --> 00:15:13,435
I calculated everything.
Don't worry, sir.

153
00:15:15,175 --> 00:15:20,205
Be like shadows, Simon. No one will
hear about you.

154
00:15:20,625 --> 00:15:25,495
Soon, lords will come. Even they should
not know who you are.

155
00:15:26,105 --> 00:15:27,495
Now...

156
00:15:27,525 --> 00:15:31,115
take your saint fabrics and leave.

157
00:15:31,765 --> 00:15:33,315
My regards.

158
00:15:41,515 --> 00:15:44,595
Don't idle around, Simon.

159
00:16:05,475 --> 00:16:07,205
Salam Alaikum, valiants.

160
00:16:07,625 --> 00:16:11,645
Alaikum Salam, Gencebay.
Gencebay!

161
00:16:12,295 --> 00:16:14,865
-How are you, brother?
-I'm good, Boran. You?

162
00:16:14,975 --> 00:16:16,515
Thank Allah.

163
00:16:17,995 --> 00:16:20,085
Mashallah!

164
00:16:23,975 --> 00:16:26,755
-How are you, Master Davud?
-Thank Allah, my valiant.

165
00:16:26,995 --> 00:16:29,535
-You too?
-I'm good.

166
00:16:29,845 --> 00:16:31,375
Alaikum Salam.

167
00:16:34,265 --> 00:16:36,775
You haven't been around.
Where were you?

168
00:16:37,065 --> 00:16:41,155
We fought the heathens in Şuşa
and Karabağ.

169
00:16:41,215 --> 00:16:43,255
Thank Allah.
Thank Allah.

170
00:16:45,135 --> 00:16:46,675
Who is this valiant?

171
00:16:46,885 --> 00:16:49,525
A Caucasian Turk.
I'm Şamil.

172
00:16:49,775 --> 00:16:53,145
I heard that Osman Bey is raising
a banner of jihad.

173
00:16:53,455 --> 00:16:55,985
I wanted to be a part of it.

174
00:16:56,995 --> 00:16:58,575
Welcome.

175
00:17:00,295 --> 00:17:02,325
You are a fortunate man, brother Şamil.

176
00:17:03,115 --> 00:17:05,675
We are going on a campaign
just as you came.

177
00:17:05,723 --> 00:17:07,535
Thank Allah.

178
00:17:07,905 --> 00:17:09,223
Good.

179
00:17:19,223 --> 00:17:21,275
There shouldn't be a problem, ladies.

180
00:17:21,723 --> 00:17:23,473
Be careful.

181
00:17:25,045 --> 00:17:28,255
They are the personal order of
the lord of Bilecik.

182
00:17:37,205 --> 00:17:40,715
Mashallah. It's shining.

183
00:17:40,975 --> 00:17:43,995
Even my eyes can see the beauty of it.

184
00:17:44,325 --> 00:17:47,915
Well done, ladies.
It's beautiful.

185
00:17:53,485 --> 00:17:55,305
Good day, ladies.

186
00:17:55,345 --> 00:17:57,425
Thank you, Bala Hatun.

187
00:17:57,505 --> 00:17:59,015
Aygül.

188
00:18:00,305 --> 00:18:02,175
They are the best products.

189
00:18:03,635 --> 00:18:05,635
It's all completed.

190
00:18:06,025 --> 00:18:07,575
Mashallah.

191
00:18:12,745 --> 00:18:15,815
Look at my mother.
She is still working.

192
00:18:16,915 --> 00:18:21,475
She never rests.
She begins as the sun shines.

193
00:18:24,095 --> 00:18:26,595
-May Allah give her strength.
-Amin.

194
00:18:26,885 --> 00:18:28,755
Amin. Amin.

195
00:18:30,195 --> 00:18:33,625
It shouldn't be talked about but
her pain is growing.

196
00:18:35,515 --> 00:18:38,285
She keeps going to the healer
for her back.

197
00:18:43,375 --> 00:18:45,255
Oh, my beautiful mother!

198
00:18:47,905 --> 00:18:49,205
Bala!

199
00:18:49,245 --> 00:18:52,325
-What would we do without you?
-Bala, my pretty girl.

200
00:18:52,695 --> 00:18:54,035
What did you do?

201
00:18:54,345 --> 00:18:56,885
What did my children do?

202
00:18:57,325 --> 00:18:59,855
They went with their father
to drill.

203
00:19:06,635 --> 00:19:09,155
Good old days.

204
00:19:11,195 --> 00:19:16,535
Ertuğrul Ghazi would take Osman
with him to drill.

205
00:19:17,015 --> 00:19:21,585
He would teach him how to
fight, how to ambush.

206
00:19:24,915 --> 00:19:27,525
I have limited breaths to take
in this world.

207
00:19:28,145 --> 00:19:30,185
Some advice from your mother.

208
00:19:30,455 --> 00:19:33,665
Raise your sons like warriors...

209
00:19:34,275 --> 00:19:38,325
and your angelic daughters
as a hatun.

210
00:19:40,945 --> 00:19:45,765
The greatest legacy of a parent
is raising a good child.

211
00:19:46,735 --> 00:19:48,045
Look.

212
00:19:48,285 --> 00:19:54,335
Osman expanded Ertuğrul Ghazi's
home.

213
00:19:54,765 --> 00:20:01,215
Now, Orhan and Alahaddin will
expand it even more.

214
00:20:01,515 --> 00:20:03,055
Inshallah.

215
00:20:05,835 --> 00:20:12,135
Mongols, Crusaders...
These wars tired us out.

216
00:20:12,905 --> 00:20:15,615
It's enough suffering for the Muslims.

217
00:20:17,055 --> 00:20:21,915
Now, you have the greatest mission
for better tomorrows.

218
00:20:22,695 --> 00:20:25,665
Raise good children.

219
00:20:28,395 --> 00:20:32,135
Go to your jobs now.

220
00:21:39,885 --> 00:21:41,465
My Allah.

221
00:21:43,355 --> 00:21:44,915
My Allah.

222
00:21:45,675 --> 00:21:49,265
Grow the fire of jihad
in my heart.

223
00:21:50,385 --> 00:21:51,775
My Allah.

224
00:21:52,745 --> 00:21:54,115
You...

225
00:21:55,105 --> 00:21:58,405
grow the fire of jihad
in my heart.

226
00:22:04,825 --> 00:22:06,155
My Allah!

227
00:22:08,305 --> 00:22:11,095
Destine me with victories!

228
00:22:11,485 --> 00:22:14,195
Destine me with conquests!

229
00:22:16,365 --> 00:22:17,905
Amin, my Allah!

230
00:22:20,285 --> 00:22:22,795
Amin, my Allah!
Amin.

231
00:22:35,965 --> 00:22:37,465
My bey.

232
00:22:38,405 --> 00:22:40,435
I'm coming from İnegöl's marketplace.

233
00:22:41,065 --> 00:22:45,595
Simon is bringing the goods.
They'll come behind the green hillside.

234
00:22:47,325 --> 00:22:48,835
Good.

235
00:22:49,035 --> 00:22:51,565
Let them come.

236
00:22:53,145 --> 00:22:54,535
My bey.

237
00:22:55,385 --> 00:22:59,005
It's good that they come.
But...

238
00:23:00,495 --> 00:23:02,595
where are our alps?

239
00:23:05,915 --> 00:23:08,255
No.
My bey...

240
00:23:09,395 --> 00:23:11,915
will we ambush the whole
caravan on our own?

241
00:23:13,115 --> 00:23:15,685
What is it, Cerkutay?
Are you afraid?

242
00:23:17,485 --> 00:23:20,025
I came here, trusting you.

243
00:23:20,065 --> 00:23:23,895
My bey. Thank you.
Let's die if you say so.

244
00:23:24,855 --> 00:23:26,565
Let's die, but...

245
00:23:27,925 --> 00:23:30,005
Where is my old Cerkutay?

246
00:23:30,825 --> 00:23:32,865
Years made you too old.

247
00:23:34,495 --> 00:23:36,575
Where is that brave Cerkutay?

248
00:23:36,925 --> 00:23:39,515
-Where is that crazy Cerkutay?
-My bey!

249
00:23:40,255 --> 00:23:42,815
I'll strike them all on my own, my bey.

250
00:23:42,955 --> 00:23:45,465
You trusted me.

251
00:23:45,535 --> 00:23:47,575
I'll turn the world into hell
for them.

252
00:23:48,225 --> 00:23:50,775
This is it!

253
00:23:51,335 --> 00:23:53,905
Mashallah to my Cerkutay.

254
00:24:06,625 --> 00:24:08,625
Go now.

255
00:24:09,405 --> 00:24:11,205
As you order, my bey.

256
00:24:11,235 --> 00:24:13,125
Godspeed.

257
00:24:13,155 --> 00:24:15,195
Thank you, my bey.
Thank you.

258
00:24:31,905 --> 00:24:33,455
Alps!

259
00:24:34,845 --> 00:24:36,405
Welcome.

260
00:24:36,565 --> 00:24:38,735
Thank you, my bey.

261
00:24:44,015 --> 00:24:47,045
He is just as I heard about his renown.
Look at this valiant!

262
00:24:53,745 --> 00:24:54,865
Alps!

263
00:24:57,345 --> 00:25:02,165
For the love of
the three, the seven, and the forty!

264
00:25:03,465 --> 00:25:06,475
-Are you ready for jihad?
-We are!

265
00:25:08,965 --> 00:25:12,005
Are you ready for jihad?
-We are!

266
00:25:12,685 --> 00:25:16,245
-What is jihad for?
-For Allah's approval!

267
00:25:16,765 --> 00:25:20,305
-Are you ready to be a ghazi?
-We are!

268
00:25:21,035 --> 00:25:23,625
-Are you ready to be a martyr?
-We are!

269
00:25:24,035 --> 00:25:28,795
Allahu Akbar!
Allahu Akbar!

270
00:25:28,945 --> 00:25:30,525
Allah is immortal!

271
00:25:30,555 --> 00:25:32,065
Allah is righteous!

272
00:25:47,155 --> 00:25:50,475
To be honest, I never
wanted peace.

273
00:25:50,785 --> 00:25:54,315
But we are profiting from it the most.

274
00:25:55,975 --> 00:26:00,565
We are trading with Osman.
He'll bring me a lot of goods soon.

275
00:26:01,665 --> 00:26:07,695
I'm sure that he is mad that he is
trading with us and not fighting.

276
00:26:10,635 --> 00:26:14,165
I don't even want to hear Osman's name.

277
00:26:15,505 --> 00:26:17,745
Aren't you old friends?

278
00:26:17,925 --> 00:26:21,495
Old friends can be enemies too, Vasilius.

279
00:26:22,825 --> 00:26:25,205
Nikola is a close witness.

280
00:26:27,955 --> 00:26:30,245
We fought a lot with Osman.

281
00:26:30,375 --> 00:26:34,845
But still, you feel better with
people of the same blood...

282
00:26:35,455 --> 00:26:38,825
same faith, same language.

283
00:26:42,095 --> 00:26:44,185
Dear Vasilius.

284
00:26:44,645 --> 00:26:49,715
Kosses returned from his mistake
even though it was late.

285
00:26:51,295 --> 00:26:55,415
Anyway, let's put these matters
aside.

286
00:26:59,185 --> 00:27:03,935
Justinianus and I have great
news for you.

287
00:29:24,485 --> 00:29:25,875
Brother.

288
00:29:41,650 --> 00:29:43,740
Orhan! Alahaddin!

289
00:29:46,490 --> 00:29:48,220
Don't go far!

290
00:29:51,810 --> 00:29:53,640
Baysungur Alp!

291
00:29:56,640 --> 00:29:58,640
We let it run away.

292
00:30:29,180 --> 00:30:30,680
Dear lords...

293
00:30:31,400 --> 00:30:33,940
We grow our friendship with Basilleus.

294
00:30:34,260 --> 00:30:36,360
I'm marrying his stepdaughter Holofira.

295
00:30:36,880 --> 00:30:39,020
You are all invited to the wedding.

296
00:30:39,020 --> 00:30:41,020
I congratulate you.

297
00:30:41,620 --> 00:30:44,620
Your ties are stronger now.

298
00:30:44,920 --> 00:30:48,990
These lands need this.
For peace.

299
00:30:49,580 --> 00:30:52,640
Peace. Peace is very important.
Yes.

300
00:30:53,160 --> 00:30:59,450
As you know, others also live
in these lands.

301
00:30:59,690 --> 00:31:06,200
So, we need to grow peace
and stability with them too.

302
00:31:06,410 --> 00:31:08,920
I think he is talking about Turks.

303
00:31:10,140 --> 00:31:15,560
We've been living in peace
with Turks for long years.

304
00:31:15,560 --> 00:31:17,560
True.

305
00:31:17,820 --> 00:31:21,920
This wedding will strengthen our ties.

306
00:31:22,810 --> 00:31:29,230
And for this reason, Turks, Osman Bey,
Turgut Bey...

307
00:31:29,520 --> 00:31:36,890
Barkın Bey, and all big Turkish beys
will be invited.

308
00:31:37,050 --> 00:31:43,130
They should come. So that the peace
can last forever.

309
00:31:46,240 --> 00:31:47,770
Good.

310
00:31:48,840 --> 00:31:51,390
Very good idea.

311
00:31:51,600 --> 00:31:54,650
So, why didn't you inform me
sooner?

312
00:31:56,970 --> 00:32:01,160
Or maybe you should've informed
me when you are informing the Turks.

313
00:32:02,110 --> 00:32:06,920
It seems like I'm as far away from
you as them.

314
00:32:09,960 --> 00:32:12,130
Michael Kosses.
Please don't think that.

315
00:32:12,800 --> 00:32:14,530
It all happened suddenly.

316
00:32:14,540 --> 00:32:17,040
Otherwise, you would hear it first.

317
00:32:17,610 --> 00:32:21,710
Justinianus.
Justinianus.

318
00:32:22,380 --> 00:32:26,580
You know it, I love you
as if you are my own nephew.

319
00:32:28,370 --> 00:32:30,460
But I'm still mad.

320
00:32:30,970 --> 00:32:34,870
Because all preperations have to
be done in a hurry.

321
00:32:37,030 --> 00:32:40,380
I can't let people say that
great Micahel Kosses...

322
00:32:40,380 --> 00:32:42,890
came to Justinianus'
wedding empty-handed!

323
00:32:45,210 --> 00:32:47,000
Pardon me, lords.

324
00:32:47,090 --> 00:32:49,640
I'm in a hurry.

325
00:33:32,070 --> 00:33:33,570
Come on.

326
00:33:49,050 --> 00:33:52,610
My dear friends, this will be a wedding
to remember.

327
00:33:52,660 --> 00:33:54,040
It'll be amazing.

328
00:33:54,040 --> 00:33:56,570
Osman's head will be a great present.

329
00:33:56,570 --> 00:33:58,370
Not only Osman.

330
00:33:58,490 --> 00:34:01,240
I hope that he'll come
with his family.

331
00:34:01,650 --> 00:34:08,070
My stepdaughter and Justinianus,
lord of Bilecik are getting married.

332
00:34:08,550 --> 00:34:14,510
Osman and his family's death will
be the greatest present to this marriage.

333
00:34:14,570 --> 00:34:15,889
Not only Osman.

334
00:34:15,889 --> 00:34:19,750
Gündüz, Turgut, their wives,
their children!

335
00:34:19,750 --> 00:34:23,070
Everyone! All of them will die!

336
00:34:23,070 --> 00:34:27,820
Only one person will left standing.

337
00:34:28,330 --> 00:34:29,920
And that's Barkın.

338
00:34:30,290 --> 00:34:31,800
Barkın?

339
00:34:33,730 --> 00:34:35,730
You trust Barkın.

340
00:34:35,780 --> 00:34:37,360
I understand that.

341
00:34:37,449 --> 00:34:40,719
Do you trust Kosses?

342
00:34:41,690 --> 00:34:44,969
Kosses is a very old friend of mine.

343
00:34:47,449 --> 00:34:53,739
And I know him enough to
not trust him, Basilleus.

344
00:34:55,550 --> 00:34:57,050
What will we do?

345
00:34:57,800 --> 00:34:59,330
What will we do?

346
00:34:59,330 --> 00:35:02,340
Kosses haven't talked to Osman
all these times.

347
00:35:02,600 --> 00:35:09,160
But still, he has something in him
for Osman... He likes him.

348
00:35:09,180 --> 00:35:11,740
We must consider this.

349
00:35:12,870 --> 00:35:14,400
So...

350
00:35:14,780 --> 00:35:18,630
to end the war before it starts,
a little price...

351
00:35:18,860 --> 00:35:24,570
Just before the wedding, Kosses
will die.

352
00:35:46,390 --> 00:35:49,460
Caravan leader, this is the
end of the road.

353
00:35:49,660 --> 00:35:52,130
No, it ends in İnegöl.

354
00:35:56,890 --> 00:35:58,440
You say so?

355
00:35:58,440 --> 00:36:01,620
We have a peace treaty.
This road belongs to all of us.

356
00:36:01,740 --> 00:36:05,800
But if you value your lives,
get out of our way.

357
00:36:05,900 --> 00:36:09,520
Your goods and lives
are at our mercy now.

358
00:36:10,930 --> 00:36:16,240
I don't waste my time speaking in a
situation that I can solve with my sword.

359
00:36:16,510 --> 00:36:18,080
Soldiers!

360
00:36:18,170 --> 00:36:21,190
It's been a long time since
we spilled Turkish blood.

361
00:36:21,280 --> 00:36:22,610
Attack!

362
00:37:36,100 --> 00:37:38,280
Come here!

363
00:37:41,640 --> 00:37:43,210
Wait here.

364
00:37:55,040 --> 00:37:56,550
Simon.

365
00:37:58,580 --> 00:38:00,140
Come here.

366
00:38:00,530 --> 00:38:02,040
Come here.

367
00:38:02,685 --> 00:38:05,235
Where are you running to
without the ammunition?

368
00:38:06,445 --> 00:38:09,185
So, you are bringing weapons
to kill Turks?

369
00:38:10,955 --> 00:38:13,525
Your intention is to
break the peace, huh?

370
00:38:14,085 --> 00:38:16,675
But the only place you can run
to...

371
00:38:17,025 --> 00:38:18,785
is my wrath.

372
00:38:19,825 --> 00:38:22,335
Kill me.
Kill me.

373
00:38:22,785 --> 00:38:27,345
No. No.
You will live.

374
00:38:28,315 --> 00:38:33,115
And you'll tell Nikola that I attacked
the caravan.

375
00:38:33,955 --> 00:38:38,355
If he considers it as breaking
the peace...

376
00:38:39,035 --> 00:38:40,835
tell him that...

377
00:38:41,295 --> 00:38:44,095
I'll use these weapons
as evidence.

378
00:38:46,005 --> 00:38:48,075
He should face me if he
has the heart.

379
00:38:48,865 --> 00:38:50,185
Come on.

380
00:38:55,515 --> 00:38:56,815
Mother.

381
00:38:56,845 --> 00:39:00,715
Food is handed out to the people
in the tribe and in Söğüt.

382
00:39:00,715 --> 00:39:02,215
Everyone is fed.

383
00:39:02,575 --> 00:39:05,155
Well done, my pretty girl.

384
00:39:05,155 --> 00:39:08,165
There isn't anyone hungry.
Thank Allah.

385
00:39:08,735 --> 00:39:10,265
Thank Allah.

386
00:39:10,265 --> 00:39:13,335
No one will be left hungry
under Osman Bey's rule.

387
00:39:13,335 --> 00:39:14,665
Inshallah.

388
00:39:15,095 --> 00:39:17,815
What did our mighty prophet
Muhammed said?

389
00:39:18,145 --> 00:39:21,665
''The one who sleep full when their
neighbor is hungry, isn't one of us.''

390
00:39:21,665 --> 00:39:24,105
May Allah destine us to be
one of them.

391
00:39:24,105 --> 00:39:26,585
Amin.
Amin.

392
00:39:26,585 --> 00:39:28,305
Livelihood turns plenty
when shared.

393
00:39:28,305 --> 00:39:30,305
May it be plentiful.

394
00:39:30,305 --> 00:39:31,895
Inshallah.

395
00:39:31,895 --> 00:39:35,985
Seeing you like this pleases me.

396
00:39:36,575 --> 00:39:37,875
I know...

397
00:39:38,495 --> 00:39:42,145
our tribe is protected by
the valiant ladies of Kayı.

398
00:39:45,125 --> 00:39:48,845
Mother. Look here.

399
00:39:49,475 --> 00:39:50,825
Come.

400
00:39:51,835 --> 00:39:53,855
Is it as you wanted?

401
00:39:56,435 --> 00:39:58,975
Mashallah, my pretty girl.

402
00:39:59,045 --> 00:40:01,635
It's very good.
Well done.

403
00:40:01,705 --> 00:40:03,285
Thank you, mother.

404
00:40:04,735 --> 00:40:06,895
With the name of Allah.

405
00:40:07,285 --> 00:40:10,705
This isn't our hand. It's the
hand of our Mother Fatma.

406
00:40:10,705 --> 00:40:14,535
May it be plentiful.

407
00:40:15,355 --> 00:40:17,355
Amin.

408
00:40:17,505 --> 00:40:19,345
Here, my girl.

409
00:40:19,905 --> 00:40:22,445
May Allah bless your hands
and mouth, mother.

410
00:40:22,955 --> 00:40:26,775
We are almost ready for iftar.

411
00:40:27,225 --> 00:40:29,035
With the name of Allah.

412
00:40:32,575 --> 00:40:35,145
Söğüt is also provided with meals.

413
00:40:35,585 --> 00:40:38,165
söğüt is also provided with meals, mother.

414
00:40:38,255 --> 00:40:41,825
They will all eat it at iftar.

415
00:40:42,855 --> 00:40:45,425
Thank you, my pretty girl.

416
00:41:05,075 --> 00:41:06,945
Leave me alone!

417
00:41:32,665 --> 00:41:34,535
Leave me alone!

418
00:41:57,285 --> 00:41:59,145
My God, protect me!

419
00:43:23,225 --> 00:43:25,265
Ya Allah!

420
00:43:45,755 --> 00:43:47,305
We won't hurt you.

421
00:43:47,305 --> 00:43:48,865
We want to help.

422
00:43:52,925 --> 00:43:55,015
There is no time.
Let's go.

423
00:44:11,605 --> 00:44:13,155
Where did they come from?

424
00:44:21,345 --> 00:44:22,685
Here.

425
00:44:22,685 --> 00:44:25,035
Get in there.

426
00:44:41,455 --> 00:44:42,825
Damn it!

427
00:44:44,735 --> 00:44:46,625
We can't go before finding her.

428
00:44:46,625 --> 00:44:48,425
Hurry! Spread out!

429
00:44:57,105 --> 00:44:58,485
Come on.

430
00:45:04,675 --> 00:45:06,035
Here.

431
00:45:34,915 --> 00:45:37,175
Söğüt

432
00:45:40,785 --> 00:45:43,165
Behold! Osman Bey!

433
00:45:45,785 --> 00:45:49,645
-Salam Alaikum.
-Alaikum Salam.

434
00:45:56,685 --> 00:45:58,275
Go on.

435
00:46:06,125 --> 00:46:17,645
With mighty Allah's ninety-nine names,
who fills our hearts with faith.

436
00:46:18,485 --> 00:46:21,545
With the name of Allah.

437
00:46:22,655 --> 00:46:24,955
Years have passed.

438
00:46:25,655 --> 00:46:28,095
We haven't fought for a long time.

439
00:46:28,575 --> 00:46:33,565
But we weren't idle either.

440
00:46:34,085 --> 00:46:35,965
We expanded our tribe.

441
00:46:36,615 --> 00:46:43,245
We strengthened Söğüt.
And our alps grew stronger.

442
00:46:43,935 --> 00:46:46,445
Our swords sharpened.

443
00:46:46,575 --> 00:46:48,895
We aren't the only ones who
did that, Osman Bey.

444
00:46:49,025 --> 00:46:51,595
So did the lords.
They are stronger.

445
00:46:51,795 --> 00:46:54,715
I heard that Nikola is positioning
soldiers in villages.

446
00:46:54,715 --> 00:46:56,995
One caravan comes after another.

447
00:46:57,135 --> 00:47:00,985
And he is inviting swords-for-sale
to his castle.

448
00:47:01,205 --> 00:47:03,205
The war is near, my bey.

449
00:47:05,085 --> 00:47:07,915
It shouldn't be far.

450
00:47:08,225 --> 00:47:10,615
They aren't scary.

451
00:47:10,965 --> 00:47:12,705
Now, tell me.

452
00:47:13,055 --> 00:47:14,865
Aren't you stronger?

453
00:47:16,135 --> 00:47:18,925
Didn't your trade increase
after the peace?

454
00:47:21,475 --> 00:47:23,325
If not...

455
00:47:23,585 --> 00:47:26,945
look at Barkın Bey.

456
00:47:28,145 --> 00:47:30,865
His treasury surpassed us all.

457
00:47:31,605 --> 00:47:35,325
Look at him and take an example.

458
00:47:39,955 --> 00:47:42,045
Mashallah, Barkın Bey.

459
00:47:42,065 --> 00:47:43,655
Mashallah.

460
00:47:43,875 --> 00:47:46,425
Not at all, Turgut Bey.

461
00:47:48,555 --> 00:47:53,755
Our belongings and existence is
for the future of the Turks.

462
00:47:54,415 --> 00:47:55,925
Thank you.

463
00:48:25,985 --> 00:48:28,065
Where are you going to?

464
00:48:35,175 --> 00:48:38,625
Look at these.
A few Turkmen children.

465
00:48:40,935 --> 00:48:42,955
Leave us alone!

466
00:48:44,805 --> 00:48:46,345
I will.

467
00:48:47,035 --> 00:48:51,125
But this lady is coming
with us.

468
00:48:54,415 --> 00:48:57,125
All of you are chasing one
little girl!

469
00:48:57,275 --> 00:48:58,665
Is this just?

470
00:48:58,935 --> 00:49:00,455
She doesn't want to come!

471
00:49:00,585 --> 00:49:02,265
She'll come with us!

472
00:50:00,165 --> 00:50:02,235
We don't leave the ones
in need!

473
00:50:02,365 --> 00:50:05,065
Over our dead bodies!

474
00:50:07,725 --> 00:50:10,285
There is no time to play, brats!

475
00:50:20,405 --> 00:50:22,725
Are you depending on
a single arrow?

476
00:50:24,555 --> 00:50:28,135
I'll bury you in here!
Soldiers!

477
00:51:03,275 --> 00:51:04,625
Come on!

478
00:51:19,895 --> 00:51:22,485
You did all you could.

479
00:51:22,825 --> 00:51:25,175
But I have to go with them now.

480
00:51:25,415 --> 00:51:27,915
No! We can't allow it!

481
00:51:55,445 --> 00:51:59,065
If you raise your hand,
you'll lose your heads!

482
00:51:59,555 --> 00:52:01,385
You'll pay for this!

483
00:52:09,155 --> 00:52:10,455
Alps!

484
00:52:17,695 --> 00:52:19,875
Thank you, Baysungur Alp!

485
00:52:19,905 --> 00:52:21,755
Mashallah, Baysungur Alp!

486
00:52:21,785 --> 00:52:23,635
You are just in time.

487
00:52:54,655 --> 00:52:57,175
You won't get away from me
again.

488
00:52:59,555 --> 00:53:01,345
You saw what happened.

489
00:53:09,855 --> 00:53:12,775
What if I wasn't here in time?

490
00:53:14,035 --> 00:53:16,085
What would I say to my bey?

491
00:53:16,155 --> 00:53:17,535
Tell me!

492
00:53:17,565 --> 00:53:19,065
We are alright!

493
00:53:19,095 --> 00:53:20,605
Thank Allah!

494
00:53:24,065 --> 00:53:27,185
What's your name?
Why were you running away?

495
00:53:28,195 --> 00:53:30,555
Why are you interrogating her?

496
00:53:30,625 --> 00:53:32,345
Let her catch her breath.

497
00:53:32,715 --> 00:53:34,835
They serve the lord of Yerhisar.

498
00:53:35,265 --> 00:53:37,295
My father won't be pleased.

499
00:53:37,595 --> 00:53:40,185
You know it, brother.
We are in peace.

500
00:53:44,645 --> 00:53:46,015
Come on.

501
00:53:46,295 --> 00:53:48,295
We'll talk the rest at the tribe.

502
00:53:49,125 --> 00:53:50,865
This place isn't safe.

503
00:53:50,935 --> 00:53:52,435
Alps!

504
00:53:52,545 --> 00:53:54,105
Ready the horses!

505
00:53:54,505 --> 00:53:55,875
Come on.

506
00:54:10,685 --> 00:54:12,855
But don't forget!

507
00:54:13,475 --> 00:54:15,065
Water sleeps...

508
00:54:16,455 --> 00:54:18,455
but the enemy doesn't.

509
00:54:23,235 --> 00:54:25,245
They'll prepare for sure.

510
00:54:30,555 --> 00:54:32,365
As you ordered...

511
00:54:32,975 --> 00:54:35,675
we are setting markets
everywhere.

512
00:54:35,855 --> 00:54:37,935
We are expanding our trade, my bey.

513
00:54:38,025 --> 00:54:39,605
But...

514
00:54:40,015 --> 00:54:42,275
in the smallest inconvenience...

515
00:54:43,035 --> 00:54:45,785
we don't have the power
to protect them.

516
00:54:47,315 --> 00:54:49,645
The treaty stands.

517
00:54:50,645 --> 00:54:55,745
We are protecting the markets
and the order with that treaty.

518
00:54:56,375 --> 00:55:02,935
We'll be continuing to protect our
markets with peace, not with our swords.

519
00:55:06,835 --> 00:55:10,895
Barkın Bey. Tell us, how many
alps do you have?

520
00:55:12,265 --> 00:55:18,275
Don't we have enough alps to
protect our trade?

521
00:55:18,545 --> 00:55:20,415
We have many valiants, my bey.

522
00:55:20,465 --> 00:55:21,845
But...

523
00:55:21,875 --> 00:55:24,085
drill isn't equal to experience.

524
00:55:24,165 --> 00:55:26,725
We are afraid that they'll get rusty
without action.

525
00:55:26,725 --> 00:55:28,815
We won't get rusty...

526
00:55:30,305 --> 00:55:32,375
or die in our tents.

527
00:55:35,945 --> 00:55:38,465
Your alps will always be ready.

528
00:55:39,235 --> 00:55:43,245
Their drills will be difficult.
They will be made of steel.

529
00:55:43,975 --> 00:55:45,565
Beys...

530
00:55:46,035 --> 00:55:48,045
not only Barkın Bey...

531
00:55:48,655 --> 00:55:52,215
you too, beys.
You too.

532
00:55:53,235 --> 00:55:56,025
After all, the one who works
the most during peacetime...

533
00:55:57,375 --> 00:55:59,595
bleeds the least during wartime.

534
00:56:01,055 --> 00:56:05,615
Not only your soldiers.
You'll prepare your sisters too.

535
00:56:07,895 --> 00:56:11,425
If there will be a war
as you say...

536
00:56:12,905 --> 00:56:14,915
we'll be ready for it.

537
00:56:16,095 --> 00:56:17,605
But...

538
00:56:17,835 --> 00:56:20,675
the treaty stands for now.

539
00:56:25,025 --> 00:56:27,865
We won't be the one to betray it.

540
00:56:35,305 --> 00:56:37,985
O' Kayı Tribe.

541
00:56:38,355 --> 00:56:42,365
When the children left,
it turned too silent.

542
00:56:43,285 --> 00:56:45,305
Soon, mother.

543
00:56:45,525 --> 00:56:49,605
When we send the goods to Bilecik,
we'll go after them.

544
00:56:51,235 --> 00:56:55,265
-Haven't they returned yet?
-No, not yet.

545
00:56:55,645 --> 00:56:57,535
We would hear it.

546
00:56:57,775 --> 00:56:59,215
Have you seen them, Aygül?

547
00:56:59,365 --> 00:57:02,485
They must be hunting with Osman Bey.

548
00:57:04,335 --> 00:57:07,375
As I see Orhan and Alahaddin...

549
00:57:07,735 --> 00:57:10,265
the fire in my heart
burns more.

550
00:57:11,725 --> 00:57:13,795
The longing of my Aktemur...

551
00:57:14,685 --> 00:57:16,695
it hurts my heart, mother.

552
00:57:17,175 --> 00:57:19,205
Patience, my girl.
Patience.

553
00:57:20,245 --> 00:57:22,295
No news?

554
00:57:22,335 --> 00:57:24,895
-Isn't he returning?
-No, Bala.

555
00:57:25,675 --> 00:57:28,255
I'm informed that there is
still time.

556
00:57:28,545 --> 00:57:29,915
Not yet.

557
00:57:32,035 --> 00:57:35,695
All those years. We haven't
even seen his face.

558
00:57:36,675 --> 00:57:40,515
Your test is very difficult, sister.
May Allah give you patience.

559
00:57:40,635 --> 00:57:42,405
Amin. Inshallah.

560
00:57:43,935 --> 00:57:45,435
Amin.

561
00:58:34,635 --> 00:58:36,165
Who is that?

562
00:58:36,605 --> 00:58:38,695
Orhan and Alahaddin?

563
00:58:38,785 --> 00:58:40,515
Yes, mother.

564
00:58:40,985 --> 00:58:43,245
There is a girl coming with them.

565
00:58:48,785 --> 00:58:52,285
Children share the fate
of their ancestors, they say.

566
00:58:52,685 --> 00:58:55,825
Did Orhan already hunted
a big hunt?

567
00:58:56,145 --> 00:58:57,445
Yes.

568
00:59:30,015 --> 00:59:31,215
My child.

569
00:59:31,225 --> 00:59:32,735
Are you alright?

570
00:59:32,735 --> 00:59:34,285
I am, mother.

571
00:59:34,375 --> 00:59:37,225
Son, what happened?
Are you alright?

572
00:59:42,095 --> 00:59:44,095
Who is our guest?

573
00:59:57,345 --> 00:59:59,095
Tell me, son.

574
00:59:59,165 --> 01:00:01,705
Weren't you drilling with your father?

575
01:00:01,835 --> 01:00:03,165
We did.

576
01:00:03,245 --> 01:00:05,065
But then we went to hunting.

577
01:00:05,125 --> 01:00:06,665
When we were hunting...

578
01:00:06,685 --> 01:00:08,735
we found her getting
chased by soldiers.

579
01:00:13,655 --> 01:00:15,075
We helped her.

580
01:00:20,175 --> 01:00:22,295
Welcome, my girl.

581
01:00:24,205 --> 01:00:25,705
Malhun.

582
01:00:26,715 --> 01:00:31,215
Let our children catch their
breaths. They'll speak.

583
01:00:31,235 --> 01:00:33,605
Let's get to the tent.

584
01:00:33,645 --> 01:00:35,195
Bring the girl.

585
01:00:35,385 --> 01:00:36,775
Come on.

586
01:00:40,635 --> 01:00:42,435
Come on, son.
Come on.

587
01:00:45,195 --> 01:00:46,925
Welcome.

588
01:00:48,245 --> 01:00:49,565
Come.

589
01:00:51,795 --> 01:00:53,175
Come on.

590
01:01:01,055 --> 01:01:04,615
Baysungur. Tell me what happened.

591
01:01:05,485 --> 01:01:07,965
We went to the riverside to
hunt rabbits.

592
01:01:08,225 --> 01:01:11,825
She was getting chased.
We attacked them.

593
01:01:16,305 --> 01:01:19,455
Yarhisar Castle

594
01:01:20,565 --> 01:01:24,895
Holofira...
Holofira...

595
01:01:30,575 --> 01:01:31,905
Sir.

596
01:01:33,225 --> 01:01:34,785
Holofira ran away.

597
01:01:35,715 --> 01:01:37,295
We couldn't find her.

598
01:01:53,865 --> 01:01:56,095
How could you let her go?

599
01:01:57,375 --> 01:02:00,445
Couldn't you control
a little girl?

600
01:02:02,035 --> 01:02:03,465
We caught her...

601
01:02:05,215 --> 01:02:07,565
some people from the Kayı Tribe
stopped us.

602
01:02:09,775 --> 01:02:11,295
We fought.

603
01:02:15,275 --> 01:02:19,165
Then, they took Holofira and
ran away.

604
01:02:33,435 --> 01:02:35,015
Osman.

605
01:02:38,255 --> 01:02:40,035
Osman!

606
01:02:49,115 --> 01:02:52,985
Go and bring Holofira to me!

607
01:03:27,105 --> 01:03:28,495
My girl.

608
01:03:30,325 --> 01:03:32,155
Are you alright?

609
01:03:35,495 --> 01:03:36,995
Good.

610
01:03:39,635 --> 01:03:42,375
Now, no one can hurt you here.

611
01:03:43,695 --> 01:03:46,225
But, firstly, tell us.

612
01:03:46,395 --> 01:03:48,425
Who are you?
Who is chasing you?

613
01:03:54,415 --> 01:03:55,735
Don't be afraid.

614
01:03:56,465 --> 01:03:58,255
This is Kayı Tribe.

615
01:03:58,995 --> 01:04:01,105
You must've heard about us.

616
01:04:07,015 --> 01:04:08,375
Tell us.

617
01:04:08,555 --> 01:04:11,725
So that we'll know who to
protect you from.

618
01:04:20,515 --> 01:04:22,925
Behold! Osman Bey!

619
01:04:29,405 --> 01:04:30,825
Salam Alaikum.

620
01:04:32,195 --> 01:04:34,375
Alaikum Salam, my bey.

621
01:04:34,375 --> 01:04:35,705
Son.

622
01:04:43,875 --> 01:04:45,235
Come.

623
01:05:04,445 --> 01:05:05,995
Welcome.

624
01:05:12,275 --> 01:05:14,015
Who is our daughter?

625
01:05:15,055 --> 01:05:17,625
Orhan and Alahaddin found her
in the forest, my bey.

626
01:05:18,625 --> 01:05:21,485
Poor girl was running away
from the lord's soldiers.

627
01:05:22,105 --> 01:05:24,695
They saved the girl with
Baysungur Alp.

628
01:05:39,235 --> 01:05:42,295
She didn't speak ever since
she arrived, son.

629
01:05:42,845 --> 01:05:44,725
She is scared.

630
01:05:46,875 --> 01:05:49,915
Tell me. What's your name?

631
01:05:50,395 --> 01:05:52,265
Where are you coming from?

632
01:05:54,425 --> 01:05:57,605
She was running away from
Yerhisar soldiers, father.

633
01:06:01,755 --> 01:06:03,095
My name is...

634
01:06:04,885 --> 01:06:06,225
Holofira.

635
01:06:09,295 --> 01:06:11,535
I'm the step-daughter of the lord
of Yerhisar.

636
01:06:15,505 --> 01:06:17,235
Why are you running away?

637
01:06:18,415 --> 01:06:22,205
My step-father is forcing me to marry
the lord of Bilecik.

638
01:06:24,545 --> 01:06:27,135
I'm not even old enough to marry.

639
01:06:30,055 --> 01:06:31,645
I don't want it.

640
01:06:31,955 --> 01:06:35,125
Haven't you told your step-father
that you don't want it?

641
01:06:35,125 --> 01:06:36,425
Of course I did.

642
01:06:37,265 --> 01:06:40,295
But he said that he can't refuse
the emperor's orders.

643
01:06:40,555 --> 01:06:43,135
He is sacrificing me to get
the emperor's favor.

644
01:06:54,165 --> 01:06:55,715
It's the azan.

645
01:06:56,015 --> 01:06:57,585
Let's end our fasting.

646
01:06:59,085 --> 01:07:00,955
We'll talk.

647
01:07:05,365 --> 01:07:06,885
My sheik.

648
01:07:15,115 --> 01:07:16,435
My Allah.

649
01:07:19,925 --> 01:07:22,815
We are fasting for your approval...

650
01:07:23,465 --> 01:07:27,535
and we are ending it with the
food you are giving.

651
01:07:28,535 --> 01:07:30,075
Approve us.

652
01:07:30,075 --> 01:07:31,385
Amin.

653
01:07:31,385 --> 01:07:36,415
You see everything and
you hear everything.

654
01:07:37,505 --> 01:07:40,775
-Accept our fasting.
-Amin.

655
01:07:40,775 --> 01:07:42,655
Amin.

656
01:07:51,665 --> 01:07:54,855
Come on now.
Enjoy it. With the name of Allah.

657
01:08:29,540 --> 01:08:32,279
İnegöl Castle

658
01:08:47,335 --> 01:08:49,365
I said that no one will enter!

659
01:08:53,205 --> 01:08:56,935
My best student, Nikola!

660
01:09:01,055 --> 01:09:02,944
Haven't you missed me?

661
01:09:05,165 --> 01:09:06,555
Your departure...

662
01:09:08,185 --> 01:09:10,734
made me really mad.

663
01:09:19,835 --> 01:09:21,205
Your return...

664
01:09:23,335 --> 01:09:24,675
made me happy.

665
01:09:28,955 --> 01:09:32,135
After all, I don't like peace.

666
01:09:34,024 --> 01:09:36,055
You were right about Kosses.

667
01:09:37,024 --> 01:09:39,415
It'll be best to kill him.

668
01:09:40,585 --> 01:09:45,135
So, my men and Yarhisar soldiers
set an ambush.

669
01:09:46,064 --> 01:09:51,604
Kosses was always close
to Osman.

670
01:09:53,774 --> 01:09:56,525
He just didn't know that
we knew it.

671
01:09:56,845 --> 01:09:59,905
And I wouldn't take such a risk.

672
01:09:59,905 --> 01:10:03,145
That wedding.
It'll be wedding.

673
01:10:03,915 --> 01:10:06,015
And it'll bring Osman's end.

674
01:10:59,065 --> 01:11:02,825
Your departure extended this
period a lot.

675
01:11:03,825 --> 01:11:06,675
I left these lands to Barkın
and you.

676
01:11:07,155 --> 01:11:11,495
I found you stronger than ever
when I returned.

677
01:11:12,275 --> 01:11:13,825
When Osman dies...

678
01:11:14,305 --> 01:11:17,065
Barkın will take over Söğüt.

679
01:11:17,745 --> 01:11:19,125
Barkın?

680
01:11:23,505 --> 01:11:25,325
The one who holds Söğüt...

681
01:11:25,975 --> 01:11:28,525
holds the leashes
of the Turks.

682
01:11:29,775 --> 01:11:34,365
Do you think the other beys
will follow Barkın?

683
01:11:34,845 --> 01:11:37,555
He has been working for this
all these years.

684
01:11:38,175 --> 01:11:43,265
Barkın is as valuable as Osman
for them.

685
01:11:46,855 --> 01:11:48,245
Good.

686
01:11:50,635 --> 01:11:55,025
Then, this will be over today.

687
01:11:55,745 --> 01:11:57,045
No.

688
01:11:57,325 --> 01:12:02,605
If you don't cut it from the
root, it'll sprout gain.

689
01:12:04,115 --> 01:12:06,225
We'll take their roots out.

690
01:12:06,375 --> 01:12:08,225
We'll take their children.

691
01:12:08,785 --> 01:12:12,325
I'll kill them in Bilecik,
in front of Osman's eyes.

692
01:12:13,725 --> 01:12:15,805
When it's all over...

693
01:12:16,155 --> 01:12:19,035
everyone will follow Barkın.

694
01:12:20,125 --> 01:12:22,195
And Barkın will obey us.

695
01:12:25,535 --> 01:12:27,415
No one enters--

696
01:12:43,565 --> 01:12:45,925
What happened to my ammunition?

697
01:12:47,055 --> 01:12:48,755
Sir, the caravan...

698
01:12:50,235 --> 01:12:54,765
It seems to me that your ammunition
is gone, Nikola.

699
01:13:00,485 --> 01:13:03,289
Harmankaya Castle

700
01:13:04,625 --> 01:13:08,395
Thank you for answering my invitation,
Justinianus.

701
01:13:10,245 --> 01:13:12,945
It's been a long time since
we talked personally.

702
01:13:13,805 --> 01:13:15,345
True.

703
01:13:17,055 --> 01:13:19,925
I assume that this foziness is
because of the wedding.

704
01:13:20,645 --> 01:13:22,195
It's the wedding.

705
01:13:22,895 --> 01:13:24,725
You are right, Kosses.

706
01:13:25,625 --> 01:13:28,175
You are just like your uncle.

707
01:13:29,555 --> 01:13:34,605
Whenever I see you, I remember your
uncle Rogatus.

708
01:13:36,555 --> 01:13:38,075
My old friend.

709
01:13:40,055 --> 01:13:41,945
A great warrior...

710
01:13:43,085 --> 01:13:45,115
and a very loyal friend.

711
01:13:46,965 --> 01:13:48,745
I miss him.

712
01:13:49,205 --> 01:13:52,905
I wish he could be with us
in your happy day.

713
01:13:55,695 --> 01:13:58,285
I don't want you in my wedding, Kosses.

714
01:13:59,255 --> 01:14:00,585
What?

715
01:14:02,085 --> 01:14:05,995
Why? I thought I was
your family.

716
01:14:06,495 --> 01:14:08,295
You were my uncle's friend.

717
01:14:08,835 --> 01:14:11,105
You are my friend too, but...

718
01:14:14,425 --> 01:14:16,635
I don't want you to come
to my wedding.

719
01:14:20,045 --> 01:14:23,095
I see, Justinianus.
I won't come to your wedding.

720
01:14:24,515 --> 01:14:27,105
But will you tell me why?

721
01:14:27,335 --> 01:14:29,345
There is no reason, Kosses.

722
01:14:30,515 --> 01:14:34,605
If you want to give me a present,
not coming will be the best present.

723
01:14:36,685 --> 01:14:38,005
I see.

724
01:14:44,905 --> 01:14:48,795
Osman? Will Osman come?

725
01:15:01,415 --> 01:15:02,805
A trap.

726
01:15:04,705 --> 01:15:07,215
They set a trap for Osman.

727
01:15:09,155 --> 01:15:11,165
Thank Allah.

728
01:15:12,595 --> 01:15:15,685
We are in another Ramadan.

729
01:15:15,715 --> 01:15:17,285
Thank Allah.

730
01:15:18,555 --> 01:15:27,575
Let's hope that Allah is pleased
with our efforts.

731
01:15:27,915 --> 01:15:30,225
Amin. Amin, my sheik.

732
01:15:33,795 --> 01:15:39,695
Do you know what Allah
says about this month?

733
01:15:40,685 --> 01:15:44,105
When Ramadan comes...

734
01:15:45,015 --> 01:15:47,185
the gates of heaven
gets opened...

735
01:15:47,925 --> 01:15:50,575
the gates of hell
gets closed...

736
01:15:51,035 --> 01:15:55,335
and the demons get chained.

737
01:15:59,775 --> 01:16:01,595
Now, you say that...

738
01:16:02,285 --> 01:16:09,925
when the demons are chained,
no sins are committed!

739
01:16:10,895 --> 01:16:16,505
If it was always devil who
deceived us...

740
01:16:17,215 --> 01:16:20,585
there is no one to stop in
our way...

741
01:16:21,925 --> 01:16:25,835
it's time for comfort
for the Muslims!

742
01:16:26,405 --> 01:16:32,775
But if you look around,
or look at yourselves...

743
01:16:33,165 --> 01:16:37,055
humans commit many sins.

744
01:16:39,855 --> 01:16:41,095
But, my sheik...

745
01:16:41,835 --> 01:16:45,055
if Allah's prophet says that they
are chained, they are chained.

746
01:16:46,715 --> 01:16:49,305
What makes us commit these sins?

747
01:16:50,365 --> 01:16:54,335
It's our desires, my shehzad.
Our desires.

748
01:16:57,525 --> 01:17:01,025
It's more cunning than the devil.

749
01:17:02,345 --> 01:17:06,385
Our Allah chains the demons
in this month...

750
01:17:06,845 --> 01:17:11,425
but we should chain
our desires too.

751
01:17:13,325 --> 01:17:14,645
My sheik.

752
01:17:16,145 --> 01:17:19,645
How can we chain our desires?
How can we discipline it?

753
01:17:20,705 --> 01:17:23,295
I kill all the heathens...

754
01:17:23,575 --> 01:17:25,655
but not my desires.

755
01:17:26,185 --> 01:17:29,595
Every person's nature
and desire is different.

756
01:17:30,385 --> 01:17:35,245
For example, some finds the salaat
difficult...

757
01:17:36,055 --> 01:17:38,905
some finds the fasting difficult.

758
01:17:40,235 --> 01:17:44,745
Some finds giving alms difficult...

759
01:17:45,215 --> 01:17:49,715
the others find
the jihad scary...

760
01:17:51,055 --> 01:17:53,275
and think that pilgrimage is difficult.

761
01:17:54,425 --> 01:17:58,035
We should look into ourselves.

762
01:17:58,555 --> 01:18:03,795
Whichever of them is the most difficult
one for us...

763
01:18:04,135 --> 01:18:07,695
we'll be more busy with it.

764
01:18:08,845 --> 01:18:14,365
Apart from what's a religious duty,
we'll do supererogatory prayers.

765
01:18:15,485 --> 01:18:18,485
We'll give alms...

766
01:18:19,315 --> 01:18:22,805
to control the stinginess
of our desires.

767
01:18:25,205 --> 01:18:30,745
We'll do supererogatory prayers
to control the conceit of our desires.

768
01:18:31,525 --> 01:18:37,095
After Ramadan, we'll
keep fasting...

769
01:18:37,635 --> 01:18:41,375
to control the lust of our desires.

770
01:18:43,305 --> 01:18:48,095
Now, tell me. What is the
greatest battle of a Muslim?

771
01:18:49,805 --> 01:18:51,625
It's their battle with their desires.

772
01:18:52,965 --> 01:18:54,515
Mashallah.

773
01:19:00,535 --> 01:19:03,885
Then, are you ready
to fight your desires?

774
01:19:05,145 --> 01:19:08,135
Thank Allah, my sheik.

775
01:19:18,825 --> 01:19:20,145
Speak.

776
01:19:21,955 --> 01:19:23,355
Sir, Osman...

777
01:19:25,285 --> 01:19:27,855
he found our secret route.

778
01:19:28,255 --> 01:19:30,345
Osman...

779
01:19:31,875 --> 01:19:33,675
found our secret route?

780
01:19:36,555 --> 01:19:40,575
How can Osman learn something that
only two of us knew?

781
01:19:40,575 --> 01:19:44,325
How? Tell me, Simon!

782
01:19:45,095 --> 01:19:46,425
How?

783
01:19:48,595 --> 01:19:49,925
How?

784
01:19:52,775 --> 01:19:55,035
I don't know, sir.

785
01:19:55,035 --> 01:19:58,055
Our soldiers. Weapons.
They are all gone.

786
01:19:58,055 --> 01:20:00,055
I will kill him!

787
01:20:00,285 --> 01:20:02,295
You can't do anything!

788
01:20:02,295 --> 01:20:03,885
Anything!

789
01:20:03,885 --> 01:20:07,995
You can't do anything when
you have this traitor in you!

790
01:20:07,995 --> 01:20:10,545
Anything!

791
01:20:13,955 --> 01:20:16,175
Tell me! Who?

792
01:20:18,425 --> 01:20:20,265
Who said it?

793
01:20:39,485 --> 01:20:41,575
When will the new
goods come?

794
01:20:42,115 --> 01:20:44,115
The caravan is on the way.

795
01:20:44,165 --> 01:20:45,895
We'll receive them tonight.

796
01:20:46,195 --> 01:20:47,735
Tonight?

797
01:20:52,185 --> 01:20:54,225
That Turkish merchant.

798
01:20:54,575 --> 01:20:58,105
With my helper...
Damn it!

799
01:20:58,775 --> 01:21:01,365
That idiot must've spoken!

800
01:21:03,675 --> 01:21:05,005
Good.

801
01:21:05,515 --> 01:21:14,095
Then, you know who to kill
before Osman, Simon!

802
01:21:22,935 --> 01:21:25,495
Will we attack, sir?

803
01:21:26,915 --> 01:21:32,085
Simon... Simon...

804
01:21:34,435 --> 01:21:38,235
Why do you think I gather
all these ammunation for?

805
01:21:38,235 --> 01:21:39,555
Why?

806
01:21:39,665 --> 01:21:41,175
For nothing?

807
01:21:41,195 --> 01:21:43,215
We won't act openly!

808
01:21:43,215 --> 01:21:45,275
We won't!

809
01:21:45,525 --> 01:21:48,175
Do you understand it, Simon?

810
01:21:48,965 --> 01:21:53,135
-Yes.
-Out, Simon. Out.

811
01:22:20,395 --> 01:22:22,615
Idiots!

812
01:22:27,555 --> 01:22:29,425
May I enter, my bey?

813
01:22:29,755 --> 01:22:31,095
Come.

814
01:22:36,925 --> 01:22:40,435
My bey, Yerhisar's lord
sent someone.

815
01:22:59,305 --> 01:23:00,655
Let him come.

816
01:23:18,775 --> 01:23:22,275
Yerhisar's lord Basilius sent
his regards.

817
01:23:27,025 --> 01:23:30,845
Lord Bailius wants his daughter Holofira.

818
01:23:31,735 --> 01:23:33,595
Please, don't give me.

819
01:23:37,635 --> 01:23:40,215
Please, don't give me!
Please!

820
01:23:51,955 --> 01:23:56,935
As you see, Holofira is our guest.

821
01:24:00,435 --> 01:24:02,785
And she has spoken.

822
01:24:03,095 --> 01:24:04,915
She doesn't want to come with you.

823
01:24:05,075 --> 01:24:07,235
But, Osman Bey, Lord Basilius--

824
01:24:07,235 --> 01:24:08,765
Get out of my sight!

825
01:24:21,245 --> 01:24:23,275
I'm grateful.

826
01:24:36,605 --> 01:24:41,155
Emperors never meddle with the
marriages of the lords.

827
01:24:43,965 --> 01:24:45,475
Holofira.

828
01:24:50,095 --> 01:24:52,375
Tell me all about it from
the beginning.

829
01:25:02,175 --> 01:25:04,545
You brought prosperity
to the bey's table.

830
01:25:05,015 --> 01:25:06,595
Thank you.

831
01:25:07,375 --> 01:25:13,175
Today, Osman Bey asked a question
at the council.

832
01:25:13,765 --> 01:25:22,835
He asked if we have the might
to protect all our markets.

833
01:25:23,985 --> 01:25:25,855
Now, I ask you.

834
01:25:26,395 --> 01:25:28,915
-Tell me.
-Barkın Bey.

835
01:25:29,395 --> 01:25:32,155
Our tribe is in prosperity,
just like your table.

836
01:25:32,155 --> 01:25:34,335
So is the numbers of our alps.

837
01:25:34,335 --> 01:25:36,365
Ergün Bey is right.

838
01:25:36,375 --> 01:25:39,395
Numbers of our alps have surpassed
many other tribes.

839
01:25:39,515 --> 01:25:43,535
We have the might to protect all the
markets including Söğüt.

840
01:25:43,615 --> 01:25:44,985
Thank you.

841
01:25:45,185 --> 01:25:47,035
-Thank you.
-Thank Allah.

842
01:25:47,255 --> 01:25:49,095
You made me happy.

843
01:25:49,215 --> 01:25:50,515
Thank you.

844
01:25:50,935 --> 01:25:54,465
But tell me...

845
01:25:55,045 --> 01:25:58,545
who has the future
of the Turks?

846
01:26:01,135 --> 01:26:06,255
Whoever feeds us has
our loyalty.

847
01:26:06,365 --> 01:26:08,795
Barkın Bey has
the future of the Turks.

848
01:26:08,995 --> 01:26:12,045
Barkın Bey.
We follow Barkın Bey.

849
01:26:12,045 --> 01:26:14,235
We are loyal to Barkın Bey.

850
01:26:14,315 --> 01:26:16,015
May I enter, my bey.

851
01:26:16,015 --> 01:26:17,385
Come.

852
01:26:47,335 --> 01:26:48,915
Gencebay.

853
01:26:50,145 --> 01:26:52,685
What did you do in your homeland?
Tell us.

854
01:26:52,795 --> 01:26:56,695
We ran after the tyrants as if
we were running after dogs!

855
01:26:59,615 --> 01:27:01,655
They didn't expect it.

856
01:27:01,825 --> 01:27:03,525
We fought fiercely.

857
01:27:03,605 --> 01:27:06,875
We didn't leave them space.
We avanged the innocent.

858
01:27:07,095 --> 01:27:09,645
The tyrants learned it well, brothers.

859
01:27:10,395 --> 01:27:13,955
If you hurt the innocent,
this is what you get.

860
01:27:15,535 --> 01:27:17,815
Play your kopuz, brother.

861
01:27:18,065 --> 01:27:19,595
Feed our souls.

862
01:27:49,815 --> 01:27:52,555
Trouble always finds us.

863
01:27:52,985 --> 01:27:56,035
Some people prove to be brave.

864
01:27:56,035 --> 01:28:02,345
Hundreds of Moses become a wall
against the modern Pharoahs.

865
01:28:02,345 --> 01:28:08,595
Ibrahims fight against the
Nimrods of this century.

866
01:28:08,595 --> 01:28:14,815
Every side of the world,
in the dungeons of the tyrants...

867
01:28:14,815 --> 01:28:20,855
thousands of alps are ready
for independence.

868
01:28:20,855 --> 01:28:27,095
Turk means hope.

869
01:28:27,095 --> 01:28:33,325
Laws orders,
when that holy day comes...

870
01:28:33,325 --> 01:28:39,455
the game ends when the Turks
come to the battlefield.

871
01:28:39,455 --> 01:28:46,155
The treacherous order gets
destroyed when the Turks come.

872
01:28:57,715 --> 01:29:03,995
Even if they always set ambushes,
the enemy can't get to us.

873
01:29:04,025 --> 01:29:10,315
Turks love their creator, and they are
the nightmare of the tyrants.

874
01:29:10,315 --> 01:29:16,335
Turks march on the righteous path,
as all traps get destroyed.

875
01:29:16,335 --> 01:29:22,415
Almighty Allah, ensure us,
strengthen our army.

876
01:29:22,415 --> 01:29:28,415
Take the world, give it to the Turks.
Let Turan become a state.

877
01:29:28,415 --> 01:29:34,845
Make our state fair and just,
make it the head of the world.

878
01:29:34,845 --> 01:29:40,855
They founded many states,
armies of wolf banners.

879
01:29:40,855 --> 01:29:47,025
The enemies of the Turks get
questioned by Almighty Allah.

880
01:29:47,025 --> 01:29:53,125
The enemies of the Islam get
questioned by Almighty Allah.

881
01:29:53,125 --> 01:29:59,235
They founded many states,
armies of wolf banners.

882
01:29:59,235 --> 01:30:05,415
The enemies of the Turks get
questioned by Almighty Allah.

883
01:30:05,415 --> 01:30:10,915
Almighty Allah questions the enemy
of Islam.

884
01:30:10,915 --> 01:30:13,975
-Praise be!
-Praise be!

885
01:30:28,685 --> 01:30:30,755
Can we come in, Osman Bey?

886
01:30:31,965 --> 01:30:33,695
Come in, brother!

887
01:30:40,565 --> 01:30:42,345
We have no time.

888
01:30:42,745 --> 01:30:46,045
I wouldn't have come at midnight if it
wasn't so important.

889
01:30:47,965 --> 01:30:49,345
What is it?

890
01:30:50,845 --> 01:30:54,885
You are invited to the Yarhisar Lord and
Bilecik Lord's wedding tomorrow.

891
01:30:56,405 --> 01:30:58,245
Don't go.

892
01:30:58,485 --> 01:31:01,585
It is a trap. They are going to kill you.

893
01:31:08,795 --> 01:31:11,035
Devil!

894
01:31:13,205 --> 01:31:15,475
I have helped him all this time.

895
01:31:16,605 --> 01:31:18,915
I saved his life many times.

896
01:31:19,895 --> 01:31:21,285
But...

897
01:31:25,985 --> 01:31:27,985
...no loyalty...

898
01:31:28,975 --> 01:31:30,365
...none.

899
01:31:33,135 --> 01:31:35,445
The devil has his army but...

900
01:31:36,745 --> 01:31:39,265
...we have our mighty friendship.

901
01:31:41,975 --> 01:31:43,845
Thank you, Kosses.

902
01:31:43,855 --> 01:31:45,635
I won't forget this favor of yours.

903
01:31:45,635 --> 01:31:46,945
Thank you.

904
01:31:47,675 --> 01:31:51,345
So, what will you do?

905
01:32:02,165 --> 01:32:05,545
You left untimely, you come untimely.

906
01:32:06,955 --> 01:32:10,035
However, I slept.

907
01:32:10,605 --> 01:32:12,205
I have just waited.

908
01:32:17,415 --> 01:32:20,805
But no matter what you still came.

909
01:32:25,625 --> 01:32:27,905
I keep my promise, Barkın.

910
01:32:35,915 --> 01:32:38,545
Was it worth leaving, Sir?

911
01:32:38,795 --> 01:32:40,375
I saved Jerusalem.

912
01:32:40,415 --> 01:32:42,945
Now it is time to save Rome.

913
01:32:43,505 --> 01:32:45,895
How are there?

914
01:32:45,965 --> 01:32:48,505
Argun is dead. Geyhatu is in control now.

915
01:32:48,725 --> 01:32:50,825
He is resting in delight.

916
01:32:50,825 --> 01:32:52,665
He has no intention to fight.

917
01:32:52,735 --> 01:32:54,965
If you are asking these lands...

918
01:32:55,085 --> 01:32:56,845
...you will help me.

919
01:32:56,845 --> 01:32:59,425
I can't be İbrahim Faki anymore.

920
01:32:59,485 --> 01:33:01,485
I've built this trust so hard.

921
01:33:01,865 --> 01:33:03,945
Just to break Osman.

922
01:33:04,135 --> 01:33:06,215
Tell me, what will I do?

923
01:33:06,225 --> 01:33:08,385
First, you will tell me about the tribe.

924
01:33:08,385 --> 01:33:10,605
What happened to whom?

925
01:33:10,605 --> 01:33:12,725
What did the last years do to Kayı?

926
01:33:12,905 --> 01:33:14,685
What did it do?

927
01:33:14,705 --> 01:33:16,225
It strengthened it.

928
01:33:16,225 --> 01:33:19,745
Where does the iron from Nikola's mine go?

929
01:33:20,085 --> 01:33:22,175
I've been wondering this for years
as well.

930
01:33:22,175 --> 01:33:23,705
But I couldn't find out.

931
01:33:23,765 --> 01:33:26,805
Did the light dazzle you, Barkın?

932
01:33:26,805 --> 01:33:28,385
It made you blind.

933
01:33:28,685 --> 01:33:32,005
Remember that those in the dark always
see.

934
01:33:33,885 --> 01:33:35,725
What will be our move?

935
01:33:36,415 --> 01:33:40,605
Our move will be to solve this problem
radically.

936
01:33:41,695 --> 01:33:46,285
Osman will be murdered at
the wedding in Bilecik.

937
01:33:46,915 --> 01:33:50,785
Why are you interested in mines if Osman
is going to die?

938
01:33:51,125 --> 01:33:53,715
For you, Barkın. For you.

939
01:33:55,455 --> 01:33:57,285
For your state.

940
01:33:59,805 --> 01:34:01,695
What will I do?

941
01:34:02,445 --> 01:34:05,395
Osman will die. His children will die.

942
01:34:05,565 --> 01:34:07,775
Kosses will die.

943
01:34:08,635 --> 01:34:11,225
You will take Söğüt.

944
01:34:13,305 --> 01:34:17,175
And will be the sole ruler of the Turks.

945
01:34:32,925 --> 01:34:35,735
The wedding is built for us.

946
01:34:36,445 --> 01:34:38,325
What are you saying, my Bey?

947
01:34:39,275 --> 01:34:41,015
Is it a trap?

948
01:34:41,555 --> 01:34:45,315
They will try to kill us at the wedding.
But...

949
01:34:46,385 --> 01:34:50,965
...they are using Holofira to lure us
to the trap.

950
01:34:54,565 --> 01:34:56,375
Those dogs!

951
01:34:56,585 --> 01:35:00,345
They waited all these years and decided
to attack now?

952
01:35:03,245 --> 01:35:07,515
What kind of a father would involve his
child in this dirty game?

953
01:35:09,135 --> 01:35:11,725
They couldn't beat us openly.

954
01:35:12,445 --> 01:35:14,915
They kept getting close all these years.

955
01:35:15,365 --> 01:35:17,595
Just to get to our backs, Osman Bey!

956
01:35:22,605 --> 01:35:26,195
Good, my Bey.
You say knowledge is everything.

957
01:35:26,195 --> 01:35:28,745
Then, we won't give Holofira.

958
01:35:29,225 --> 01:35:31,105
We won't send the goods as well.

959
01:35:31,135 --> 01:35:34,575
Then, we will organize an expedition
to Bilecik at the first opportunity.

960
01:35:34,575 --> 01:35:35,845
No.

961
01:35:37,355 --> 01:35:40,885
Actually, now we will give Holofira to his
father.

962
01:35:45,315 --> 01:35:47,065
She will go to the wedding.

963
01:35:47,505 --> 01:35:52,545
We will drink the sherbet of martyrdom
instead of the poisoned sherbet.

964
01:35:57,445 --> 01:35:59,725
We will both give them the wedding
gifts...

965
01:35:59,995 --> 01:36:01,495
...and take the castle.

966
01:36:01,785 --> 01:36:04,285
And take the Holofira too and return.

967
01:36:16,815 --> 01:36:20,405
The war is at our door, Selvi.

968
01:36:21,785 --> 01:36:24,345
Osman is terribly cornered.

969
01:36:25,945 --> 01:36:27,665
His and...

970
01:36:28,945 --> 01:36:32,125
...those with him are near to their end.

971
01:36:33,655 --> 01:36:35,735
What is in your mind?

972
01:36:35,905 --> 01:36:37,945
What should we do, Barkın?

973
01:36:40,465 --> 01:36:42,495
We will think about ourselves.

974
01:36:43,065 --> 01:36:45,645
We will protect your fathers' legacy.

975
01:36:46,325 --> 01:36:50,185
Our heads will always stay up.

976
01:36:50,985 --> 01:36:53,985
We won't fight for Osman but for
ourselves.

977
01:36:54,045 --> 01:36:58,605
If necessary, we will be against Osman.

978
01:37:00,105 --> 01:37:02,105
What are you saying, Barkın?

979
01:37:02,145 --> 01:37:04,805
Osman Bey has always been so good to us.

980
01:37:05,285 --> 01:37:07,695
If we've been living here in peace
all this time...

981
01:37:07,695 --> 01:37:09,705
...Osman Bey's share in this is quite big.

982
01:37:09,705 --> 01:37:13,495
Osman Bey's only wish was to make us
thankful to him, my Selvi.

983
01:37:13,685 --> 01:37:15,725
We took what was ours.

984
01:37:15,805 --> 01:37:17,875
He thinks he granted it.

985
01:37:18,625 --> 01:37:20,805
I want to live in peace, Barkın.

986
01:37:21,005 --> 01:37:23,125
I don't want to get separated.

987
01:37:24,505 --> 01:37:26,595
Oh, my beautiful Hatun.

988
01:37:27,345 --> 01:37:30,385
Osman never saw us as one of his own.

989
01:37:30,605 --> 01:37:32,845
He rose above by stepping on us.

990
01:37:33,015 --> 01:37:37,105
It is enough. It is our turn to rise.

991
01:37:39,365 --> 01:37:41,085
Let's talk about this later.

992
01:37:41,095 --> 01:37:43,625
There is a wedding, we shouldn't be late.
Come on.

993
01:37:44,045 --> 01:37:45,545
No, Selvi!

994
01:37:47,765 --> 01:37:49,845
I don't let you to the wedding.

995
01:37:50,825 --> 01:37:52,595
I am leaving now.

996
01:37:52,785 --> 01:37:55,845
You think thoroughly about what we talked.

997
01:37:56,125 --> 01:37:59,855
Think until you share the same decision
as me, Selvi.

998
01:38:12,115 --> 01:38:14,005
This is dangerous.

999
01:38:15,055 --> 01:38:17,115
How many people are involved...

1000
01:38:17,455 --> 01:38:19,485
...how many soldiers are waiting for us...

1001
01:38:20,205 --> 01:38:21,965
...the other Lords invited...

1002
01:38:22,165 --> 01:38:24,265
We finalized our decision, Konur.

1003
01:38:25,655 --> 01:38:27,105
If we know the trap...

1004
01:38:28,495 --> 01:38:31,205
...they will be the ones to get trapped.

1005
01:38:35,875 --> 01:38:42,805
Right! We will go with the alps and
destroy the castle and those dogs!

1006
01:38:43,075 --> 01:38:44,405
No.

1007
01:38:44,605 --> 01:38:46,965
If we go with the alps...

1008
01:38:47,335 --> 01:38:49,585
...they will see that we are aware of
the trap.

1009
01:38:53,595 --> 01:38:55,805
You will go.

1010
01:38:58,545 --> 01:39:01,425
We will conquer the castle with Kayı's
Hatuns.

1011
01:39:02,635 --> 01:39:04,795
And Bilecik Castle will be ours.

1012
01:39:07,085 --> 01:39:10,015
We will share the spoils we took
from there...

1013
01:39:10,015 --> 01:39:11,465
...with our army.

1014
01:39:11,465 --> 01:39:13,465
We will encourage our army.

1015
01:39:13,465 --> 01:39:16,025
We will dress them with swords.

1016
01:39:18,905 --> 01:39:23,445
We will walk to İnegol with
the preparations we have made...

1017
01:39:23,985 --> 01:39:26,255
... all this time.

1018
01:39:32,505 --> 01:39:34,815
The women have been waiting for this day.

1019
01:39:35,505 --> 01:39:38,095
They have been waiting to fight.

1020
01:39:38,425 --> 01:39:40,515
Thankfully, it is time!

1021
01:39:41,415 --> 01:39:47,475
No move, no wall, no trap...

1022
01:39:48,055 --> 01:39:50,125
...can't stand before us anymore!

1023
01:39:53,095 --> 01:39:59,145
It is time for war. Time to conquer!

1024
01:41:26,805 --> 01:41:28,695
Protect me, God!

1025
01:42:10,725 --> 01:42:13,565
I thought we were friends, Osman Bey.

1026
01:42:19,265 --> 01:42:22,185
What made you think otherwise, Basileus?

1027
01:42:22,185 --> 01:42:23,575
Tell me.

1028
01:42:24,245 --> 01:42:26,275
What you did yesterday.

1029
01:42:28,225 --> 01:42:29,735
You retained my daughter.

1030
01:42:33,515 --> 01:42:37,525
You were supposed to send her to me.

1031
01:42:40,775 --> 01:42:42,275
Basileus...

1032
01:42:43,045 --> 01:42:46,155
...if I had delivered your daughter to
someone else and not you...

1033
01:42:47,345 --> 01:42:49,775
...our friendship would be damaged.

1034
01:42:52,435 --> 01:42:54,005
In that case...

1035
01:42:55,315 --> 01:42:59,325
...I hope you will honor our friendship.

1036
01:43:00,705 --> 01:43:02,535
I will take Holofira and leave.

1037
01:43:43,305 --> 01:43:44,645
Sure.

1038
01:43:46,325 --> 01:43:48,845
Sure, I will deliver you what
you entrusted to me.

1039
01:43:53,475 --> 01:43:55,305
-Boran!
-My Bey.

1040
01:43:57,425 --> 01:43:59,165
Bring Holofira.

1041
01:44:00,505 --> 01:44:02,095
As you order, my Bey.

1042
01:44:09,215 --> 01:44:11,045
Don't be afraid.

1043
01:45:19,635 --> 01:45:24,935
You will make me very happy if you come
to my daughter's wedding...

1044
01:45:25,665 --> 01:45:28,575
...with your whole family, Osman Bey.

1045
01:45:29,185 --> 01:45:33,575
Please don't reject my intivation.

1046
01:45:40,875 --> 01:45:42,675
Thank you.

1047
01:45:43,185 --> 01:45:45,655
Since you invite us to the wedding...

1048
01:45:46,575 --> 01:45:51,415
...of course, we will accept
the invitation.

1049
01:46:47,195 --> 01:46:49,565
The dog showed its face, Boran.

1050
01:46:50,305 --> 01:46:54,575
It is time to be a wolf against that dog.

1051
01:46:56,785 --> 01:46:59,335
We will destroy their traps upon them!

1052
01:47:00,575 --> 01:47:02,115
As you order, my Bey.

1053
01:47:08,945 --> 01:47:11,305
As Osman falls into the trap of the Lords
...

1054
01:47:11,615 --> 01:47:13,625
...we will achieve our goal.

1055
01:47:14,535 --> 01:47:16,565
Find me such men that...

1056
01:47:17,495 --> 01:47:19,585
...they hold the dead in their palms.

1057
01:47:20,635 --> 01:47:22,145
As you order, my Bey.

1058
01:47:22,575 --> 01:47:25,635
I won't wait anymore. Söğüt will be mine.

1059
01:47:28,495 --> 01:47:29,995
Now go.

1060
01:47:30,095 --> 01:47:34,115
I will find out where the iron coming from
the mines go.

1061
01:47:38,785 --> 01:47:40,285
Praise be!

1062
01:47:41,515 --> 01:47:43,555
The best of blacksmith apprentices!

1063
01:47:46,985 --> 01:47:49,245
Do you know why I called you here?

1064
01:47:54,795 --> 01:47:56,305
You will make me a sword.

1065
01:47:57,455 --> 01:47:59,985
But only you.

1066
01:48:02,845 --> 01:48:04,355
Now, listen to me.

1067
01:48:18,845 --> 01:48:22,255
I wish I could come as well so that you
wouldn't be alone.

1068
01:48:23,695 --> 01:48:27,545
But one of us has to stay at the tribe
for our children, Malhun.

1069
01:48:31,775 --> 01:48:33,905
We worry about our children but...

1070
01:48:33,905 --> 01:48:37,925
...that so-called Lord doesn't show mercy
to that little girl!

1071
01:48:38,875 --> 01:48:41,705
We know her father but what about her
mother?

1072
01:48:42,135 --> 01:48:44,155
Is she alive?

1073
01:48:44,795 --> 01:48:48,005
What kind of a mother would get her child
in such a dirty game?

1074
01:48:50,945 --> 01:48:53,025
We don't know that much.

1075
01:48:54,955 --> 01:48:58,035
The girl wanted to go to Bursa, to her
aunt.

1076
01:48:59,705 --> 01:49:01,755
How good you said, Bala Hatun.

1077
01:49:02,005 --> 01:49:04,505
Her only wish was to go to her aunt
safe and sound.

1078
01:49:04,795 --> 01:49:06,315
My Orhan...

1079
01:49:07,815 --> 01:49:10,325
...but the conditions prevented it.

1080
01:49:10,595 --> 01:49:13,315
You know your father did the best he
could.

1081
01:49:14,635 --> 01:49:17,085
I promised her that my father wouldn't
let her down.

1082
01:49:18,075 --> 01:49:20,135
How about that, mother Bala?

1083
01:49:27,295 --> 01:49:29,855
My soft-hearted child!

1084
01:49:30,495 --> 01:49:32,015
My Orhan...

1085
01:49:32,385 --> 01:49:34,625
...your father made the best decision.

1086
01:49:35,455 --> 01:49:37,525
Besides, maybe there is something he
knows.

1087
01:49:39,025 --> 01:49:41,125
It is not our place to criticize it.

1088
01:50:06,095 --> 01:50:07,315
Brother Orhan.

1089
01:50:13,575 --> 01:50:16,315
Brother Orhan! My Sheik Grandfather
is waiting.

1090
01:50:16,495 --> 01:50:19,435
We have a drill in the lodge. We are late!

1091
01:50:22,165 --> 01:50:24,215
Orhan! Alaaddin!

1092
01:50:33,705 --> 01:50:36,915
Take your swords. We are going to
the lodge.

1093
01:50:38,275 --> 01:50:39,615
Come on.

1094
01:51:02,455 --> 01:51:06,035
This is inside of Bilecik.

1095
01:51:07,115 --> 01:51:10,125
We get this map redrawn every time we go.

1096
01:51:11,875 --> 01:51:13,895
Since they are setting a trap for us...

1097
01:51:13,925 --> 01:51:16,465
...we are taking measures.

1098
01:51:18,765 --> 01:51:21,295
When we are at the saloon with Turgut Bey
...

1099
01:51:21,815 --> 01:51:25,085
...you will disperse around.

1100
01:51:26,205 --> 01:51:27,445
-Boran.
-My Bey.

1101
01:51:27,445 --> 01:51:28,785
Konur.

1102
01:51:28,825 --> 01:51:31,915
You will keep close to the Lords'
Commanders.

1103
01:51:32,385 --> 01:51:36,835
You will kill them without an order
at their first move.

1104
01:51:36,985 --> 01:51:38,505
As you order, my Bey.

1105
01:51:39,605 --> 01:51:41,175
Be careful.

1106
01:51:41,275 --> 01:51:43,865
These cowards do not always attack
with a sword.

1107
01:51:43,865 --> 01:51:46,955
They won't hesitate to use poison.

1108
01:51:46,955 --> 01:51:48,335
Right.

1109
01:51:48,415 --> 01:51:52,085
Kamil, did you bring the antidote Kumral
Abdal gave you?

1110
01:51:52,085 --> 01:51:53,395
I did, my Bey.

1111
01:51:53,445 --> 01:51:54,655
Thank you.

1112
01:51:54,655 --> 01:51:56,855
Praise be that you considered every
measure.

1113
01:51:56,855 --> 01:51:59,415
-Of course!
-Thank you.

1114
01:51:59,485 --> 01:52:01,515
-Gence Bey.
-Yes, my Bey.

1115
01:52:01,625 --> 01:52:02,995
Turhan.

1116
01:52:03,455 --> 01:52:06,515
The secret passage left from Rogatus
still works.

1117
01:52:06,735 --> 01:52:09,235
You will bring the rest of the alps
through there.

1118
01:52:09,445 --> 01:52:11,025
As you order, my Bey.

1119
01:52:12,115 --> 01:52:14,675
Sisters will go inside with the goods.

1120
01:52:14,805 --> 01:52:17,335
And we will go inside via the wedding.

1121
01:53:12,875 --> 01:53:14,925
Praise be!

1122
01:53:19,615 --> 01:53:21,625
Praise be, to my valiants!

1123
01:53:25,285 --> 01:53:26,675
Come on.

1124
01:53:26,755 --> 01:53:29,295
Take the ones my Sheik finished to
the oven.

1125
01:53:31,415 --> 01:53:35,005
Allaaddin, pour some water to
my hands, son.

1126
01:53:36,385 --> 01:53:37,945
Come on.

1127
01:53:44,585 --> 01:53:47,175
Enough, enough. Thank you

1128
01:53:55,445 --> 01:53:58,555
You are tired, grandfather.
You sweat blood.

1129
01:53:58,785 --> 01:54:01,275
Wouldn't it be better to leave it
to the apprentices?

1130
01:54:01,465 --> 01:54:04,315
He that would eat the kernel must
crack the nut, son.

1131
01:54:05,115 --> 01:54:10,555
Would it suit me to be useless that I am
a Sheik?

1132
01:54:11,765 --> 01:54:16,615
I will keep working as long as
I have the strength.

1133
01:54:28,225 --> 01:54:33,265
Don't underestimate what we do, Shahzadas.

1134
01:54:33,265 --> 01:54:35,045
No way.

1135
01:54:41,505 --> 01:54:44,555
Do you know what makes a good Muslim?

1136
01:54:44,805 --> 01:54:46,655
We wish to learn, my Sheik.

1137
01:54:51,845 --> 01:54:53,195
All right, then.

1138
01:54:53,615 --> 01:54:55,475
Leave it to me, my Sheik.

1139
01:54:56,945 --> 01:54:58,665
Thank you, my Akça.

1140
01:55:07,495 --> 01:55:09,075
Sit.

1141
01:55:21,995 --> 01:55:27,005
A good Muslim is one with good actions.

1142
01:55:28,175 --> 01:55:32,455
It is to prosper the world and to be
instrumental...

1143
01:55:32,795 --> 01:55:42,495
... in good works that are beneficial
to humans, nature and animals.

1144
01:55:43,155 --> 01:55:46,975
My job is to make jugs.

1145
01:55:48,105 --> 01:55:49,885
To make pottery.

1146
01:55:51,885 --> 01:55:56,045
If good food is cooked in women's ovens...

1147
01:55:56,685 --> 01:55:59,845
...happiness comes to the home.

1148
01:56:00,395 --> 01:56:09,415
Children who eat from that pot
have strength.

1149
01:56:10,745 --> 01:56:17,565
If the pot you make betrays the meal...

1150
01:56:18,715 --> 01:56:22,805
...it will give hard time to our sister
who cooks the meal.

1151
01:56:23,585 --> 01:56:28,295
What will I do if the pottery I made
embarrasses her...

1152
01:56:28,835 --> 01:56:32,845
...to her husband? Right, my Shahzadas?

1153
01:56:36,125 --> 01:56:41,165
With this love, I make these pots.

1154
01:56:41,255 --> 01:56:45,465
With that spirit, I still work at this
age.

1155
01:56:46,705 --> 01:56:50,775
A Muslim can't lay around.

1156
01:56:52,345 --> 01:56:55,925
He must always be on duty.

1157
01:56:56,355 --> 01:56:58,215
Don't forget, sons...

1158
01:56:58,665 --> 01:57:01,725
...as a man's work is...

1159
01:57:02,335 --> 01:57:04,455
...so is his faith.

1160
01:57:04,835 --> 01:57:11,025
The work of a man who does not do
his job well and cheats...

1161
01:57:12,085 --> 01:57:16,245
...never goes well.

1162
01:57:19,105 --> 01:57:22,945
His faith is also tied by a thread.

1163
01:57:23,285 --> 01:57:28,595
You should be smart and never cheat.

1164
01:57:35,405 --> 01:57:38,515
What did I tell you just before?

1165
01:57:38,895 --> 01:57:40,955
A Muslim can't lay around, my Sheik.

1166
01:57:43,685 --> 01:57:45,755
He must always be on duty.

1167
01:57:49,665 --> 01:57:51,805
-Come on, brother.
-Come on, brother.

1168
01:57:52,895 --> 01:57:55,785
Come on. Praise be!

1169
01:58:01,065 --> 01:58:02,885
Come on, valiants!

1170
01:58:03,465 --> 01:58:06,975
Praise be to you, my boys!

1171
01:58:35,885 --> 01:58:37,435
Alps!

1172
01:58:40,295 --> 01:58:41,645
Brothers!

1173
01:58:44,635 --> 01:58:49,205
Years of peace are now coming to an end!

1174
01:58:50,065 --> 01:58:53,565
But this end is a new beginning!

1175
01:58:54,965 --> 01:58:56,995
Not it is the time of conquest!

1176
01:58:58,455 --> 01:59:00,475
Bilecik Castle will be...

1177
01:59:00,745 --> 01:59:06,035
...the property of the Turks before
the sun rises again!

1178
01:59:09,995 --> 01:59:19,535
Allahu Akbar! Allahu Akbar! Allahu Akbar!
Allahu Akbar! Allahu Akbar! Allahu Akbar!

1179
01:59:24,295 --> 01:59:25,675
Shoot!

1180
01:59:30,495 --> 01:59:32,565
They are as good as you said, Nikola.

1181
01:59:32,655 --> 01:59:36,665
Osman, Turgut, Gündüz, all of them,
all of them...

1182
01:59:36,715 --> 01:59:40,075
...will be shot by these snipers!

1183
01:59:40,545 --> 01:59:42,975
I've been laughing at Osman's face
for years.

1184
01:59:43,085 --> 01:59:44,715
It is frustrating, Nikola!

1185
01:59:44,925 --> 01:59:52,405
We will destroy all of his tribe, women
children, and his alps! All of them!

1186
01:59:52,405 --> 01:59:54,195
We will leave him with nothing!

1187
01:59:54,385 --> 01:59:58,845
Nothing at all!

1188
02:00:18,865 --> 02:00:21,355
Obviously, someone sent their dogs
after us.

1189
02:00:23,205 --> 02:00:25,205
Don't be obvious.

1190
02:00:25,995 --> 02:00:28,505
Let's continue as if we don't know.

1191
02:00:28,655 --> 02:00:30,665
Then, we will hit at the right moment.

1192
02:00:35,945 --> 02:00:39,055
Attack! I want the children alive!

1193
02:00:46,115 --> 02:00:48,305
Alps, protect the children!

1194
02:00:49,745 --> 02:00:53,025
Don't be afraid, brother! We will arrive
at the tribe safe and sound!

1195
02:00:53,025 --> 02:00:55,565
I am not afraid while you got my back,
brother!

1196
02:01:02,835 --> 02:01:08,355
We didn't do that much training for
nothing. It is time to show your skills!

1197
02:01:08,485 --> 02:01:10,235
Don't disappoint me!

1198
02:01:11,185 --> 02:01:13,455
-Come on! Allah!
-Allah!

1199
02:01:30,055 --> 02:01:34,125
Osman's weak lights!
I came to put you out!

1200
02:02:02,675 --> 02:02:07,225
Drop your sword! Or else, you will watch
your brother die!

1201
02:02:07,395 --> 02:02:09,645
-Who are you?
-I am not joking!

1202
02:02:11,515 --> 02:02:12,895
Drop it!

1203
02:02:15,975 --> 02:02:18,105
Fine! Let my brother go!

1204
02:02:20,835 --> 02:02:22,415
Take them!

1205
02:02:27,085 --> 02:02:29,145
We are going to Bilecik!

1206
02:02:34,135 --> 02:02:35,645
Alaaddin!

1207
02:02:58,135 --> 02:03:01,925
How very kind of you to come
and welcome us!

1208
02:03:02,095 --> 02:03:03,305
You are so kind.

1209
02:03:03,415 --> 02:03:07,635
Frankly, I'm not here to comrade you,
but to lead you astray.

1210
02:03:09,325 --> 02:03:10,645
Is that so?

1211
02:03:11,625 --> 02:03:13,135
Welcome.

1212
02:03:14,465 --> 02:03:17,055
The Christians have been fighting all
these years.

1213
02:03:17,275 --> 02:03:19,685
You kept being on Osman's side...

1214
02:03:19,685 --> 02:03:21,615
...while you are so different from him.

1215
02:03:21,705 --> 02:03:24,725
Osman is an honest man, Betrus.

1216
02:03:24,865 --> 02:03:26,665
That is enough for me.

1217
02:03:26,815 --> 02:03:28,625
Since you love him this much...

1218
02:03:28,755 --> 02:03:30,595
...you can die together!

1219
02:03:31,175 --> 02:03:34,705
Osman will die tonight.
We have his son, Orhan.

1220
02:03:35,925 --> 02:03:38,505
You are done, Kosses!

1221
02:03:57,025 --> 02:03:58,535
Kiros!

1222
02:04:13,205 --> 02:04:15,305
Back to back, Kiros!

1223
02:04:27,025 --> 02:04:28,845
Are you ready, Kiros?

1224
02:04:28,865 --> 02:04:30,945
I am, Lord Kosses!

1225
02:04:32,595 --> 02:04:33,915
Come on!

1226
02:04:42,225 --> 02:04:44,115
I am here, Kosses!

1227
02:04:49,695 --> 02:04:52,395
Damn it! Osman came!

1228
02:04:53,765 --> 02:04:56,065
Now you are doomed!

1229
02:05:05,905 --> 02:05:07,465
Kosses!

1230
02:05:16,225 --> 02:05:18,755
You hid them well, right?

1231
02:05:19,545 --> 02:05:21,315
They can't be seen.

1232
02:05:21,345 --> 02:05:23,375
Everything is done, Ayşe Hatun.

1233
02:05:25,045 --> 02:05:26,345
All right.

1234
02:05:32,505 --> 02:05:34,055
Malhun...

1235
02:05:34,175 --> 02:05:36,015
...you don't look well.

1236
02:05:36,065 --> 02:05:38,745
I haven't been able to
find Orhan since he left the tent.

1237
02:05:39,215 --> 02:05:41,715
He went to the lodge with Alaaddin.

1238
02:05:43,195 --> 02:05:45,925
He worried a great deal about the Lord's
daughter.

1239
02:05:46,635 --> 02:05:48,175
He was upset.

1240
02:05:49,585 --> 02:05:53,145
Malhun, your son is growing up.

1241
02:05:55,115 --> 02:05:56,895
Baysungur is with them.

1242
02:05:56,895 --> 02:06:00,455
They will return safe and sound.
Don't worry.

1243
02:06:04,345 --> 02:06:08,455
The carriages are ready to set off,
my Bala.

1244
02:06:09,575 --> 02:06:12,415
Sisters are ready as well.
They are waiting for your order.

1245
02:06:12,465 --> 02:06:13,835
Good.

1246
02:06:13,895 --> 02:06:15,745
Be careful.

1247
02:06:16,135 --> 02:06:17,845
Bless your right.

1248
02:06:18,465 --> 02:06:21,335
If I drink the sherbet of martyrdom...

1249
02:06:21,505 --> 02:06:23,555
...the children are entrusted to you.

1250
02:06:23,855 --> 02:06:25,645
Don't say that, Bala!

1251
02:06:25,715 --> 02:06:28,775
You will take Bilecik and return safely,
I hope!

1252
02:06:30,105 --> 02:06:31,655
I hope so.

1253
02:06:37,515 --> 02:06:38,855
Mother.

1254
02:06:39,995 --> 02:06:41,585
My beautiful daughter.

1255
02:06:43,225 --> 02:06:45,755
Be careful.

1256
02:06:46,125 --> 02:06:49,885
May your way be clear,
may your sword be sharp.

1257
02:06:49,885 --> 02:06:51,355
I hope so, mother.

1258
02:06:54,875 --> 02:06:56,195
Come on!

1259
02:06:56,205 --> 02:06:57,795
May Allah protect you!

1260
02:06:57,865 --> 02:06:59,255
Come on.

1261
02:07:18,675 --> 02:07:21,195
May all of you return safe and sound!

1262
02:07:22,675 --> 02:07:25,475
Bilecik Castle

1263
02:08:07,795 --> 02:08:10,615
I have been waiting for a long time,
Master Arius.

1264
02:08:10,705 --> 02:08:12,265
Welcome.

1265
02:08:12,355 --> 02:08:14,175
I didn't come empty-handed.

1266
02:08:16,745 --> 02:08:19,275
I brought you a wedding gift.

1267
02:08:24,795 --> 02:08:27,565
Nikola would be jealous.

1268
02:08:31,545 --> 02:08:34,875
Did you bring Turkish boys as wedding
gifts?

1269
02:08:37,045 --> 02:08:41,055
They are not random Turkish boys, Nikola.

1270
02:08:42,025 --> 02:08:44,545
They are Osman's sons.

1271
02:08:48,625 --> 02:08:50,195
Allaaddin.

1272
02:08:51,635 --> 02:08:53,145
Orhan.

1273
02:09:04,275 --> 02:09:08,795
Take them to the darkest part of
the dungeon.

1274
02:09:23,515 --> 02:09:25,055
Orhan!

1275
02:09:36,825 --> 02:09:40,915
Wedding preparations will continue
with all its reality.

1276
02:09:41,145 --> 02:09:45,345
They can never suspect anything.

1277
02:09:46,245 --> 02:09:48,745
Everything goes according to the plan,
Master Arius.

1278
02:09:49,335 --> 02:09:51,895
There is nothing to be suspected.

1279
02:09:52,415 --> 02:09:54,925
Osman is thinking he is coming to my
wedding.

1280
02:09:55,135 --> 02:09:56,725
But...

1281
02:09:59,865 --> 02:10:02,375
...they will come to their funeral.

1282
02:10:09,055 --> 02:10:10,375
Take them!

1283
02:10:24,735 --> 02:10:26,065
Kosses!

1284
02:10:26,175 --> 02:10:27,525
Hang on!

1285
02:10:27,765 --> 02:10:30,335
Hang on! We are taking you to Söğüt.

1286
02:10:31,565 --> 02:10:33,095
Osman Bey.

1287
02:10:34,185 --> 02:10:36,225
They took them to Bilecik!

1288
02:10:36,285 --> 02:10:37,585
Who?

1289
02:10:41,175 --> 02:10:42,565
Children.

1290
02:10:42,815 --> 02:10:44,205
They took the children!

1291
02:10:45,045 --> 02:10:46,545
Orhan...

1292
02:10:46,975 --> 02:10:48,555
...Alaaddin!

1293
02:10:52,105 --> 02:10:53,635
Who took them!

1294
02:10:54,185 --> 02:10:56,745
Who did? Kosses! Who did?

1295
02:10:59,195 --> 02:11:00,785
Kosses!

1296
02:11:14,055 --> 02:11:17,175
-Have you seen Orhan and Alaaddin?
-I didn't, Malhun Hatun.

1297
02:11:54,335 --> 02:11:55,675
My children!

1298
02:11:57,635 --> 02:11:59,395
My Allah, may you protect them!

1299
02:12:06,215 --> 02:12:07,735
Baysungur!

1300
02:12:07,795 --> 02:12:09,875
Baysungur! Baysungur!

1301
02:12:09,875 --> 02:12:11,895
Baysungur! Who did this?

1302
02:12:11,905 --> 02:12:13,495
Where are my sons?

1303
02:12:14,635 --> 02:12:15,965
They took them!

1304
02:12:19,025 --> 02:12:20,915
They took them, Malhun Hatun!

1305
02:12:20,945 --> 02:12:22,785
What are you saying, Baysungur?

1306
02:12:22,835 --> 02:12:24,855
Who took my sons?

1307
02:12:25,455 --> 02:12:28,485
They took them to Bilecik Castle!

1308
02:12:28,575 --> 02:12:29,955
Who?

1309
02:12:29,975 --> 02:12:32,985
One with a hidden face... years before...

1310
02:12:43,005 --> 02:12:45,085
Take Baysungur to the healing tent.

1311
02:12:45,095 --> 02:12:46,335
Yes, Malhun Hatun.

1312
02:12:46,405 --> 02:12:47,935
Come on. Come on.

1313
02:12:52,375 --> 02:12:55,435
Alps! Get ready!

1314
02:12:56,105 --> 02:12:57,985
We are going to Bilecik!

1315
02:13:10,035 --> 02:13:11,625
Alps!

1316
02:13:12,695 --> 02:13:14,725
Take Kosses to Söğüt!

1317
02:13:14,875 --> 02:13:16,605
Take him to my Sheik.

1318
02:13:16,685 --> 02:13:18,035
Come on, brothers!

1319
02:13:18,055 --> 02:13:19,845
Hang on, Kosses!

1320
02:13:19,885 --> 02:13:21,255
Hang on!

1321
02:13:31,075 --> 02:13:33,645
Let's enter their castle at once,
Osman Bey!

1322
02:13:33,735 --> 02:13:36,445
They will learn what's the price for
taking your children!

1323
02:13:36,855 --> 02:13:39,875
Even if my children's hair is harmed...

1324
02:13:41,025 --> 02:13:44,045
...I will destroy those Lords' castles
upon them!

1325
02:13:47,565 --> 02:13:50,075
But that is not what we will do now.

1326
02:13:50,895 --> 02:13:52,615
What?

1327
02:13:52,775 --> 02:13:55,725
-Why don't we go now, Osman Bey?
-We will.

1328
02:13:57,755 --> 02:13:59,335
We will go to the wedding.

1329
02:14:00,955 --> 02:14:04,465
We will sit on their table as if nothing
happened.

1330
02:14:07,445 --> 02:14:09,025
We will laugh.

1331
02:14:09,915 --> 02:14:13,955
We will have fun. But when the time comes
...

1332
02:14:14,435 --> 02:14:16,485
We will draw our swords and...

1333
02:14:16,625 --> 02:14:18,485
...be their wrath!

1334
02:14:19,665 --> 02:14:22,215
We will also take our children safely.

1335
02:14:22,675 --> 02:14:25,235
-Yes!
-Yes, my Bey.

1336
02:14:26,185 --> 02:14:27,735
Yes, my Bey.

1337
02:14:37,035 --> 02:14:38,405
Come on!

1338
02:15:31,105 --> 02:15:32,415
Brother!

1339
02:15:41,385 --> 02:15:42,955
Alaaddin!

1340
02:15:47,505 --> 02:15:48,815
My brother!

1341
02:16:01,885 --> 02:16:03,205
Father!

1342
02:16:13,050 --> 02:16:15,050
Don't come father.

1343
02:16:17,620 --> 02:16:18,930
Don't come.

1344
02:16:20,360 --> 02:16:22,130
Don't come, father.

1345
02:16:23,210 --> 02:16:24,600
It is a trap!

1346
02:16:28,410 --> 02:16:29,740
It is a trap!

1347
